COLLDATA("qencen","en",[[177,"§Kafir\nThe people who do not know the meaning of ‘Kafir’ consider it extremely derogatory. Let us try to understand its origin.\nThe word ‘kafir’ originates from the word ‘kufr’ which means – to cover, to hide or to reject. Because a kafir or disbeliever hides his original state or nature and rejects it, he is called a kafir. He can also be called an ‘atheist’.\nIt is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n“Every human being is born in his original state or nature, then his parents convert him into a Christian, or a Jew or Majoosi (polytheist).”\n(Bukhari, 1359 and Muslim, 2658)\nHere by original nature is meant ‘monotheism’ towards which Islam invites. Islam is the original state in which every child is born. Then the parents convert him to their faith. So, the child of Christians grows up a Christian and the child of Jews grows up into a Jew. His original nature is suppressed and curtailed.\nKufr is a terrible disease which is explained in various ways in the Holy Quran. For the opponents of Islam, the life of this world has been made alluring. The Holy Quran says:\nزُيِّنَ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا الْحَيَاةُ الدُّنْيَا وَيَسْخَرُونَ مِنَ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا ۘ وَالَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا فَوْقَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ ۗ وَاللَّهُ يَرْزُقُ مَن يَشَاءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ\nThe life of this world is alluring to those who reject faith, and they scoff at those who believe. But the righteous will be above them on the Day of Resurrection; for Allah bestows His abundance without measure on whom He will.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-212)\nThe Holy Quran describes the various reasons for Kufr in great detail. One of them is envy. The study of the ancient tribes shows that they rejected the prophets sent to them through sheer envy. The reason why the Last Prophet(saws) was rejected was also envy because they actually recognised Muhammad(saws) from various signs and prophecies in the previous religious books. The Holy Quran says:\nفَقَالَ الْمَلَأُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِن قَوْمِهِ مَا هَٰذَا إِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ يُرِيدُ أَن يَتَفَضَّلَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَلَوْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ لَأَنزَلَ مَلَائِكَةً مَّا سَمِعْنَا بِهَٰذَا فِي آبَائِنَا الْأَوَّلِينَ\nThe chiefs of the Unbelievers among his people said: \"He is no more than a man like yourselves: his wish is to assert his superiority over you: if Allah had wished (to send messengers), He could have sent down angels; never did we hear such a thing (as he says), among our ancestors of old.\"\n(Quran, Surah-23, Al-Muminoon, Verse-24)\nWhen Allah(swt) sent prophets and messengers to reform the people and recognize their original and inherent state of monotheism, the chieftains and leaders were the first ones to reject them out of envy and fear that their leadership would be in danger. The leaders of Quraish forbade the people from listening to the Holy Quran, lest they get inspired to reform and challenge their leadership. The Holy Quran says:\nوَقَالَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَا تَسْمَعُوا لِهَٰذَا الْقُرْآنِ وَالْغَوْا فِيهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَغْلِبُونَ\nThe Unbelievers say: \"Listen not to this Qur'an, but talk at random in the midst of its (reading), that ye may gain the upper hand!\"\n(Quran, Surah-41, Fussilat, Verse-26)\nThe words ‘Kufr’ and ‘Kafirs’ are used in the Holy Quran in the correct sense. These words are used as opposites of ‘Momin’ or ‘Muslims’. A Momin or Muslim is one who follows the commands of Allah(swt) and a kafir is one who refuses to follow the commands of Allah(swt) and His Messenger(saws). So, actually the first disbeliever was Iblees who refused to follow the order of Allah(swt) to prostrate in front of Adam(as) and thus became one among the disbelievers of Islam. (Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-34)\nThen, Allah(swt) kept sending messengers from time to time and the ones who rejected them started being called ‘kafirs’. For example Nuh(as) called his people to the path of Allah(swt), but they refused to believe in him and were therefore drowned in a terrible flood. The supplication of Nuh(as) at that time is described in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَقَالَ نُوحٌ رَّبِّ لَا تَذَرْ عَلَى الْأَرْضِ مِنَ الْكَافِرِينَ دَيَّارًا ٢٦ إِنَّكَ إِن تَذَرْهُمْ يُضِلُّوا عِبَادَكَ وَلَا يَلِدُوا إِلَّا فَاجِرًا كَفَّارًا ٢٧﴾\nAnd Noah, said: \"O my Lord! Leave not of the Unbelievers, a single one on earth! \"For, if Thou dost leave (any of) them, they will but mislead Thy devotees, and they will breed none but wicked ungrateful ones.\n(Quran, Surah-71, Nuh, Verses-26,27)\nIn the same way, Thamud, the tribe of Saleh(as) disbelieved his message and hamstrung and killed the camel which was sent as a sign from Allah(swt) and the retribution was this:\nكَأَن لَّمْ يَغْنَوْا فِيهَا ۗ أَلَا إِنَّ ثَمُودَ كَفَرُوا رَبَّهُمْ ۗ أَلَا بُعْدًا لِّثَمُودَ\nAh! Behold! for the Thamud rejected their Lord and Cherisher! Ah! Behold! removed (from sight) were the Thamud!\n(Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verse-68)\nAnd when Isa(as) started preaching the message of Allah(swt) to the Bani-Israel, he(as) perceived that some of the people were rejecting his message. The Holy Quran says:\nفَلَمَّا أَحَسَّ عِيسَىٰ مِنْهُمُ الْكُفْرَ قَالَ مَنْ أَنصَارِي إِلَى اللَّهِ ۖ قَالَ الْحَوَارِيُّونَ نَحْنُ أَنصَارُ اللَّهِ آمَنَّا بِاللَّهِ وَاشْهَدْ بِأَنَّا مُسْلِمُونَ\nWhen Jesus found Unbelief on their part He said: \"Who will be My helpers to (the work of) Allah?\" Said the disciples: \"We are Allah's helpers: We believe in Allah, and do thou bear witness that we are Muslims.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Aali-Imran, Verse-52)\nThat is, the people who did not believe the message of Isa(as) were termed Kafir (disbelievers or atheists).\nIn the present context, kafirs are those who do not believe in the Holy Prophet(saws) because he(saws) was sent as a messenger for the entire mankind. After him, till Doomsday no prophet will come to earth. In fact Isa(as) who was raised up alive will come back to earth and follow the religion of Muhammad(saws).\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said,\n“If Musa(as) had been alive today, even he would follow me.”\nThe rights of a kafir:\nA kafir may be living in a Muslim state or a Muslim may be living in a state where the majority are non-Muslims. In both states, it is compulsory for a Muslim to protect the life, property and dignity of a non-Muslim. It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“For the one who has killed a ‘Zimmi’ (non-Muslim living in a Muslim state), paradise is forbidden.”\nIt is clearly explained in the Holy Quran:\nلَّا يَنْهَاكُمُ اللَّهُ عَنِ الَّذِينَ لَمْ يُقَاتِلُوكُمْ فِي الدِّينِ وَلَمْ يُخْرِجُوكُم مِّن دِيَارِكُمْ أَن تَبَرُّوهُمْ وَتُقْسِطُوا إِلَيْهِمْ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُقْسِطِينَ\nAllah forbids you not, with regard to those who fight you not for (your) Faith nor drive you out of your homes, from dealing kindly and justly with them: for Allah loveth those who are just.\n(Quran, Surah-60, Al-Mumtahina, Verse-8)\nThis is because neither are the Muslims the enemies of non-Muslims nor are all the non-Muslims the enemies of Muslims. So, it is the duty of Muslims to take an active part in the progress of the country in which they live and understand that they are the representatives of Islam – the religion of Allah(swt) and they should set an example by their behavior. The Holy Quran says:\nكُنتُمْ خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخْرِجَتْ لِلنَّاسِ تَأْمُرُونَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَتَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنكَرِ وَتُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ\nYe are the best of peoples, evolved for mankind, enjoining what is right, forbidding what is wrong, and believing in Allah.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Aali-Imran, Verse-110)"],[178,"§Kafur (Camphor)\nCamphor is called ‘Kafur’ in Arabic. When it is mixed with something, it gives a pleasant fragrance. The drinks which the pious people will be served in paradise will contain camphor.\nThe Holy Quran says:\n﴿إِنَّ الْأَبْرَارَ يَشْرَبُونَ مِن كَأْسٍ كَانَ مِزَاجُهَا كَافُورًا ٥ عَيْنًا يَشْرَبُ بِهَا عِبَادُ اللَّهِ يُفَجِّرُونَهَا تَفْجِيرًا ٦﴾\nAs to the Righteous, they shall drink of a Cup (of Wine) mixed with Kafur,- A Fountain where the Devotees of Allah do drink, making it flow in unstinted abundance.\n(Quran, Surah-76, Ad-Dahar, Verses-5-6)\nThis camphor will be different from the camphor of this earth. It will be extremely sweet-smelling, tasty, soothing and enjoyable. Drinking it will gladden the soul. There will be streams of this which we can divert wherever we go. Actually we cannot imagine or describe the things of paradise very clearly as they are beyond the realm of our understanding. Allah(swt) has used the examples of the things of this world just to give us an idea and make us understand the fathomless wonders of paradise."],[179,"§Khabr\nKhabr is the hole in which the dead are buried. This is called a grave. Even the ancient Arabs buried their dead in graves. We even understand from the Taurah that the dead were buried in graves. For example Yaqub(as) who died in Egypt was first mummified (that is embalmed in herbs and perfumes) and then forty days later Yusuf(as) brought him to Palestine upon the order of Pharaoh (Firaun) and then buried in a cave in Maqfila (Genesis, 50:2,7,13)\nIn the same way, the body of Yusuf(as) was brought to Palestine from Egypt and buried there by the Bani-Israel. But if the person was diseased then the body would be burnt. (Amos 6:10). Even the Arabs buried their dead. We come to know from the ancient Hindu scriptures that the practice of burying their dead was prevalent then. (See Atharvaved 18/2/50; Shabdon ka jeevan, p-36; Author – Bholanath Tiwari)\nEven the Holy Quran commands us to bury the dead:\nثُمَّ أَمَاتَهُ فَأَقْبَرَهُ\nThen He causeth him to die, and putteth him in his grave;\n(Quran, Surah-80, Abasa, Verse-21)\n﴿أَلْهَاكُمُ التَّكَاثُرُ ١ حَتَّىٰ زُرْتُمُ الْمَقَابِرَ ٢﴾\nThe mutual rivalry for piling up (the good things of this world) diverts you (from the more serious things), Until ye visit the graves.\n(Quran, Surah-102, Al-Takaathur, Verses-1,2)\nThe grave is actually the first step of the life of the Hereafter. If somebody passes through this stage successfully (that is endures the trials of the grave easily), then the further trials are easy as is narrated in one hadith Tirmizi (2308) and Ibn-Maaja (4267).\nBefore and after the advent of Islam and even today graves form one of the main stations of shirk where the foolish people bow before and worship the dead as only Almighty Allah(swt) should be worshipped. Some even prostrate in front of the graves. All these things are completely against the teachings of Islam. That is why in the sahih hadith, the building of tombs is prohibited. (Sahih Muslim, 970)\nIt is narrated in another hadith:\n“When a pious person dies, people build a mosque over his grave and install his idol in it. These are the evil ones.”\n(Bukhari, 1341 and Muslim, 528)\nWhile prohibiting the building of tombs over graves, it is also emphasised that the graves should not be desecrated.\nIt is narrated in one Sahih Hadith:\nThe Holy Prophet said, “If a person sits on a burning coal till his clothes are burnt; it is better than sitting on a grave.” (Muslim, 971)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“Neither sit on graves nor offer salah facing them.”\n(Muslim, 972)\nIn the same way it is forbidden to walk between graves without removing footwear.\n(Abu Dawood, 3230; Nasai, 2048, Ibn-Maaja, 1568)\nThis is because just as we respect the living, we should also respect the dead. In the same way it is forbidden to break the bones of the dead and it is commanded to dig the graves deep so that the animals cannot dig out the dead bodies. In this way Islam not only commands us to respect the living but also respect the dead.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) instructs us:\n“It is among the teachings of Islam that when somebody from among you dies pray for him instead of discussing his faults.”\n(Abu Dawood, 4899)\nThe grave is dug in two ways: one is ‘Lahad’ and the other is ‘Shikh’ (Bagli).\nLahad is that type of grave which is straight as is the grave of the Holy Prophet(saws). In this, the body is placed in the grave, then covered with slates or slabs of stone and then finally covered with mud. (Muslim, 966)\nShikh is the type of grave which is dug in places where the mud is hard and the grave may cave in from the top. For example in Makka where the land is hard and rocky, these type of graves are dug. More than one dead body can be buried in one grave. For example the martyrs of the battle of Uhud were buried in one grave following the orders of the Holy Prophet(saws).\nFirst the body of the person who can recite more of the Holy Quran is placed, then the person who can recite less than him and so on. (Bukhari, 1347)\nIn this way, the Holy Prophet(saws) placed the scholars of Quran on a higher scale both in life and in death.\nThe trials of the grave:\nThe grave is the first destination of the life of the hereafter. The one who is saved from the trials of the grave will also be saved from the trials of the Doomsday and the one who does not escape the trials of the grave will not escape the trials of the Doomsday.\nThe Holy Quran says in connection with the trials of the grave:\n﴿فَوَقَاهُ اللَّهُ سَيِّئَاتِ مَا مَكَرُوا ۖ وَحَاقَ بِآلِ فِرْعَوْنَ سُوءُ الْعَذَابِ ٤٥ النَّارُ يُعْرَضُونَ عَلَيْهَا غُدُوًّا وَعَشِيًّا ۖ وَيَوْمَ تَقُومُ السَّاعَةُ أَدْخِلُوا آلَ فِرْعَوْنَ أَشَدَّ الْعَذَابِ ٤٦﴾\nThen Allah saved him from (every) ill that they plotted (against him), but the burnt of the Penalty encompassed on all sides the People of Pharaoh. In front of the Fire will they be brought, morning and evening: And (the sentence will be) on the Day that Judgment will be established: \"Cast ye the People of Pharaoh into the severest Penalty!\"\n(Quran, Surah-40, Al-Momin, Verses-45-46)\nIn another verse of the Holy Quran, it says:\nسَنُعَذِّبُهُم مَّرَّتَيْنِ ثُمَّ يُرَدُّونَ إِلَىٰ عَذَابٍ عَظِيمٍ\ntwice shall We punish them: and in addition shall they be sent to a grievous penalty.\n(Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-101)\nIt is explained clearly in surah Al-An’aam:\nوَلَوْ تَرَىٰ إِذِ الظَّالِمُونَ فِي غَمَرَاتِ الْمَوْتِ وَالْمَلَائِكَةُ بَاسِطُو أَيْدِيهِمْ أَخْرِجُوا أَنفُسَكُمُ ۖ الْيَوْمَ تُجْزَوْنَ عَذَابَ الْهُونِ بِمَا كُنتُمْ تَقُولُونَ عَلَى اللَّهِ غَيْرَ الْحَقِّ وَكُنتُمْ عَنْ آيَاتِهِ تَسْتَكْبِرُونَ\nIf thou couldst but see how the wicked (do fare) in the flood of confusion at death! - the angels stretch forth their hands, (saying),\"Yield up your souls: this day shall ye receive your reward,- a penalty of shame, for that ye used to tell lies against Allah, and scornfully to reject of His signs!\"\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al An’aam, Verse-93)\nIt is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n“When a person is buried in his grave and his people start leaving, he hears the sound of their shoes. Just then two angels appear and make him sit up and ask him as to what he knows about this person? That is about Muhammad(saws).\nThe believer says, “I bear witness that he is the slave and messenger of Allah(swt)”. Then it is said to him “You would have seen your abode in hell but Allah(swt) has changed your abode to heaven”, and he sees his abode in hell and in heaven. And when a hypocrite or a disbeliever is asked about Muhammad(saws), he will reply, “I don’t know, the people said that.” Then he will be beaten with an iron hammer and his screams are heard by everybody other than humans and the jinns.” (Bukhari, 1374)\nBecause if the humans and the jinn hear the screams, then it will be impossible to live on this earth. So, Allah(swt) has forbidden them to be heard by the humans and the jinns and the trials of the grave are a part of Imaan-bil-Ghayb."],[180,"§Kharoon\nThe description about Kharoon occurs in the Holy Quran as:\n﴿إِنَّ قَارُونَ كَانَ مِن قَوْمِ مُوسَىٰ فَبَغَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ ۖ وَآتَيْنَاهُ مِنَ الْكُنُوزِ مَا إِنَّ مَفَاتِحَهُ لَتَنُوءُ بِالْعُصْبَةِ أُولِي الْقُوَّةِ إِذْ قَالَ لَهُ قَوْمُهُ لَا تَفْرَحْ ۖ إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْفَرِحِينَ ٧٦ وَابْتَغِ فِيمَا آتَاكَ اللَّهُ الدَّارَ الْآخِرَةَ ۖ وَلَا تَنسَ نَصِيبَكَ مِنَ الدُّنْيَا ۖ وَأَحْسِن كَمَا أَحْسَنَ اللَّهُ إِلَيْكَ ۖ وَلَا تَبْغِ الْفَسَادَ فِي الْأَرْضِ ۖ إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُفْسِدِينَ ٧٧ قَالَ إِنَّمَا أُوتِيتُهُ عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِندِي ۚ أَوَلَمْ يَعْلَمْ أَنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ أَهْلَكَ مِن قَبْلِهِ مِنَ الْقُرُونِ مَنْ هُوَ أَشَدُّ مِنْهُ قُوَّةً وَأَكْثَرُ جَمْعًا ۚ وَلَا يُسْأَلُ عَن ذُنُوبِهِمُ الْمُجْرِمُونَ ٧٨ فَخَرَجَ عَلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ فِي زِينَتِهِ ۖ قَالَ الَّذِينَ يُرِيدُونَ الْحَيَاةَ الدُّنْيَا يَا لَيْتَ لَنَا مِثْلَ مَا أُوتِيَ قَارُونُ إِنَّهُ لَذُو حَظٍّ عَظِيمٍ ٧٩ وَقَالَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْعِلْمَ وَيْلَكُمْ ثَوَابُ اللَّهِ خَيْرٌ لِّمَنْ آمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا وَلَا يُلَقَّاهَا إِلَّا الصَّابِرُونَ ٨٠ فَخَسَفْنَا بِهِ وَبِدَارِهِ الْأَرْضَ فَمَا كَانَ لَهُ مِن فِئَةٍ يَنصُرُونَهُ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُنتَصِرِينَ ٨١﴾\nQarun was doubtless, of the people of Moses; but he acted insolently towards them: such were the treasures We had bestowed on him that their very keys would have been a burden to a body of strong men, behold, his people said to him: \"Exult not, for Allah loveth not those who exult (in riches). \"But seek, with the (wealth) which Allah has bestowed on thee, the Home of the Hereafter, nor forget thy portion in this world: but do thou good, as Allah has been good to thee, and seek not (occasions for) mischief in the land: for Allah loves not those who do mischief.\" He said: \"This has been given to me because of a certain knowledge which I have.\" Did he not know that Allah had destroyed, before him, (whole) generations,- which were superior to him in strength and greater in the amount (of riches) they had collected? but the wicked are not called (immediately) to account for their sins. So he went forth among his people in the (pride of his worldly) glitter. Said those whose aim is the Life of this World: \"Oh! that we had the like of what Qarun has got! for he is truly a lord of mighty good fortune!\" But those who had been granted (true) knowledge said: \"Alas for you! The reward of Allah (in the Hereafter) is best for those who believe and work righteousness: but this none shall attain, save those who steadfastly persevere (in good).\" Then We caused the earth to swallow up him and his house; and he had not (the least little) party to help him against Allah, nor could he defend himself.\n(Quran, Surah-28, Al-Qasas, Verses-76-81)\nIt is narrated in one sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said,\n“Before you, a person who strutted about the earth wrapped in a shawl was plunged in to the earth and till the Doomsday he will keep on being plunged into the earth.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 5789 and Sahih Muslim, 2088)\nAt another place in the Holy Quran it says:\n﴿وَقَارُونَ وَفِرْعَوْنَ وَهَامَانَ ۖ وَلَقَدْ جَاءَهُم مُّوسَىٰ بِالْبَيِّنَاتِ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ وَمَا كَانُوا سَابِقِينَ ٣٩ فَكُلًّا أَخَذْنَا بِذَنبِهِ ۖ فَمِنْهُم مَّنْ أَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِ حَاصِبًا وَمِنْهُم مَّنْ أَخَذَتْهُ الصَّيْحَةُ وَمِنْهُم مَّنْ خَسَفْنَا بِهِ الْأَرْضَ وَمِنْهُم مَّنْ أَغْرَقْنَا ۚ وَمَا كَانَ اللَّهُ لِيَظْلِمَهُمْ وَلَٰكِن كَانُوا أَنفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُونَ ٤٠﴾\n(Remember also) Qarun, Pharaoh, and Haman: there came to them Moses with Clear Signs, but they behaved with insolence on the earth; yet they could not overreach (Us). Each one of them We seized for his crime: of them, against some We sent a violent tornado (with showers of stones); some were caught by a (mighty) Blast; some We caused the earth to swallow up; and some We drowned (in the waters): It was not Allah Who injured (or oppressed) them:\" They injured (and oppressed) their own souls.\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verses-39-40)\nIt is narrated in one sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said,\n“The one who offers salah will have light, evidence and deliverance, on the day of Resurrection and the one who does not offer salah will have neither light nor evidence nor deliverance and on the Doomsday he will be with Kharoon, Pharaoh (Firaun), Haman and Ubaiyy-bin-Kaab.”\n(Musnad Ahmad, 2:169 and Darmi, 2:301)\nWhen Musa(as) started preaching the message of Allah(swt), Kharoon formed a group along with some people and started opposing Musa(as) and became an enemy of Bani-Israel. But Allah(swt) punished him in such a way that it became a lesson for the disbelievers till Doomsday.\nThis Kharoon is the same ‘Korah’ of the Bible whose description occurs in the book ‘Numbers’ whose gist is as follows:\nKharoon was the son of the paternal uncle of Musa(as). His father was ‘Yishaar’ and grandfather was ‘Kahaat’ and the father of Musa(as) was ‘Imran’ and grandfather was ‘Kahaat’. He became jealous of Musa(as) and Haroon(as) that they had become the leaders of Bani-Israel while he was wealthier than them. He became proud and arrogant. One day he went up to Musa(as) along with two hundred and fifty people and asked him, “All the people of Bani-Israel are pure and pious people. Why do both of you consider yourselves pure and who has made you leaders?” On receiving a sign from Allah(swt), Musa(as) asked all of them to come the next day. When they came the next day, Musa(as) asked all the other people of Bani-Israel to move away. As the people who had come with Kharoon stood watching outside their tents, Musa(as) started walking away with Kharoon when suddenly the earth split asunder and Kharoon was swallowed up along with his family. And his two hundred and fifty companions were burnt to ashes (Numbers, 16:1-35)\nIf looked at in one way, Kharoon had become the enemy of his people because he along with Pharaoh (Firaun) was opposing Musa(as), who was trying to save the Bani-Israel from the atrocities of Pharaoh (Firaun). He was proud of his wealth and could not digest the fact that Musa(as) and Haroon(as) had become the leaders of their tribe in spite of his immense wealth. From the various descriptions in the Holy Quran we understand that the tribe of Lut(as) was destroyed with a shower of stones, the tribes of Aad and Thamud with explosions, Kharoon was thrust into the earth and Pharaoh (Firaun) and Haman were drowned. In this way, the people of Mecca and ultimately the whole mankind is being warned that just as the proud, wealthy and disobedient tribes incurred the wrath of Allah(swt) for rejecting the message of His(swt) prophets, we shall also be destroyed in no time if we do not follow the message preached by the Holy Prophet(saws)."],[181,"§Kharz\nKharz means ‘loan’. In the Holy Quran and sahih hadith, the importance of giving loan to the poor and needy has been stressed and is considered a noble deed. In the Holy Quran, it is strongly recommended that we spend in the way of Allah(swt); so much so that Allah(swt) terms it as a loan to Him:\nمَّن ذَا الَّذِي يُقْرِضُ اللَّهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا فَيُضَاعِفَهُ لَهُ أَضْعَافًا كَثِيرَةً ۚ وَاللَّهُ يَقْبِضُ وَيَبْسُطُ وَإِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُونَ\nWho is he that will loan to Allah a beautiful loan, which Allah will double unto his credit and multiply many times? It is Allah that giveth (you) Want or plenty, and to Him shall be your return.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-245)\nWhat is meant by giving a beautiful loan to Allah(swt) is spending one’s wealth to spread the religion of Allah(swt) and to help the poor and needy.\nThe Holy Quran says:\nمَّن ذَا الَّذِي يُقْرِضُ اللَّهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا فَيُضَاعِفَهُ لَهُ وَلَهُ أَجْرٌ كَرِيمٌ\nWho is he that will Loan to Allah a beautiful loan? for (Allah) will increase it manifold to his credit, and he will have (besides) a liberal Reward.\n(Quran, Surah-57, Al-Hadid, Verse-11)\nIn the above verses, Allah(swt) has placed Himself in the position of the taker of a loan; that is, giving a loan to a needy person is like giving a loan to Allah(swt). This shows the importance of helping a needy person.\nAt another place in the Holy Quran, the command to spend in the way of Allah(swt) is given immediately after the order to offer salah and give zakat:\nوَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَآتُوا الزَّكَاةَ وَأَقْرِضُوا اللَّهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا ۚ وَمَا تُقَدِّمُوا لِأَنفُسِكُم مِّنْ خَيْرٍ تَجِدُوهُ عِندَ اللَّهِ هُوَ خَيْرًا وَأَعْظَمَ أَجْرًا ۚ وَاسْتَغْفِرُوا اللَّهَ ۖ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ\nEstablish regular Prayer and give regular Charity; and loan to Allah a Beautiful Loan. And whatever good ye send forth for your souls ye shall find it in Allah's Presence,- yea, better and greater, in Reward and seek ye the Grace of Allah: for Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.\n(Quran, Surah-73, Al-Muzammil, Verse-20)\nIn fact giving a loan to a needy person is a very pious deed while taking interest for the same is a great sin. Islam strives to establish a society in which the rich and the poor help each other and have a peaceful co-existence and not live as enemies. How can there exist brotherly love in a society where the rich suck the life-blood of the poor? That is why for strengthening the bonds of love and affection among mankind, it is necessary that we help out each other. That is the reason why the Holy Prophet(saws) said according to a sahih hadith:\n“Allah(swt) helps His slave when the slave helps his brother.”\n(Musnad Ahmad, 2:274)\nWhile stressing the importance of giving loan to the needy, a few rules are also laid down for the person who takes a loan:\n1. The transaction has to be committed in writing so that there is no dispute about it in future. The longest surah of the Holy Quran, Al-Baqara, describes this in great detail. If all these things are kept in mind, there will not be any doubts in future. The Holy Quran says about this:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذَا تَدَايَنتُم بِدَيْنٍ إِلَىٰ أَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى فَاكْتُبُوهُ ۚ وَلْيَكْتُب بَّيْنَكُمْ كَاتِبٌ بِالْعَدْلِ ۚ وَلَا يَأْبَ كَاتِبٌ أَن يَكْتُبَ كَمَا عَلَّمَهُ اللَّهُ ۚ فَلْيَكْتُبْ وَلْيُمْلِلِ الَّذِي عَلَيْهِ الْحَقُّ وَلْيَتَّقِ اللَّهَ رَبَّهُ وَلَا يَبْخَسْ مِنْهُ شَيْئًا ۚ فَإِن كَانَ الَّذِي عَلَيْهِ الْحَقُّ سَفِيهًا أَوْ ضَعِيفًا أَوْ لَا يَسْتَطِيعُ أَن يُمِلَّ هُوَ فَلْيُمْلِلْ وَلِيُّهُ بِالْعَدْلِ ۚ وَاسْتَشْهِدُوا شَهِيدَيْنِ مِن رِّجَالِكُمْ ۖ فَإِن لَّمْ يَكُونَا رَجُلَيْنِ فَرَجُلٌ وَامْرَأَتَانِ مِمَّن تَرْضَوْنَ مِنَ الشُّهَدَاءِ أَن تَضِلَّ إِحْدَاهُمَا فَتُذَكِّرَ إِحْدَاهُمَا الْأُخْرَىٰ ۚ وَلَا يَأْبَ الشُّهَدَاءُ إِذَا مَا دُعُوا ۚ وَلَا تَسْأَمُوا أَن تَكْتُبُوهُ صَغِيرًا أَوْ كَبِيرًا إِلَىٰ أَجَلِهِ ۚ ذَٰلِكُمْ أَقْسَطُ عِندَ اللَّهِ وَأَقْوَمُ لِلشَّهَادَةِ وَأَدْنَىٰ أَلَّا تَرْتَابُوا ۖ إِلَّا أَن تَكُونَ تِجَارَةً حَاضِرَةً تُدِيرُونَهَا بَيْنَكُمْ فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ أَلَّا تَكْتُبُوهَا ۗ وَأَشْهِدُوا إِذَا تَبَايَعْتُمْ ۚ وَلَا يُضَارَّ كَاتِبٌ وَلَا شَهِيدٌ ۚ وَإِن تَفْعَلُوا فَإِنَّهُ فُسُوقٌ بِكُمْ ۗ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ ۖ وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ اللَّهُ ۗ وَاللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ\nO ye who believe! When ye deal with each other, in transactions involving future obligations in a fixed period of time, reduce them to writing Let a scribe write down faithfully as between the parties: let not the scribe refuse to write: as Allah Has taught him, so let him write. Let him who incurs the liability dictate, but let him fear His Lord Allah, and not diminish aught of what he owes. If the party liable is mentally deficient, or weak, or unable Himself to dictate, Let his guardian dictate faithfully, and get two witnesses, out of your own men, and if there are not two men, then a man and two women, such as ye choose, for witnesses, so that if one of them errs, the other can remind her. The witnesses should not refuse when they are called on (For evidence). Disdain not to reduce to writing (your contract) for a future period, whether it be small or big: it is juster in the sight of Allah, More suitable as evidence, and more convenient to prevent doubts among yourselves but if it be a transaction which ye carry out on the spot among yourselves, there is no blame on you if ye reduce it not to writing. But take witness whenever ye make a commercial contract; and let neither scribe nor witness suffer harm. If ye do (such harm), it would be wickedness in you. So fear Allah; For it is Good that teaches you. And Allah is well acquainted with all things. If ye are on a journey, and cannot find a scribe, a pledge with possession (may serve the purpose). And if one of you deposits a thing on trust with another, let the trustee (faithfully) discharge his trust, and let him Fear his Lord conceal not evidence; for whoever conceals it, - his heart is tainted with sin. And Allah knoweth all that ye do.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-282)\nIn the preceding verses, the taking of interest is severely criticised. In fact the one who takes interest is warned that he should get ready to fight Allah(swt) and His Messenger(saws).\nActually Allah(swt) has stressed the importance of loan and a good loan (Karz-e-Hasna) so that society is rid of the disease of interest. When interest is forbidden, the poor and needy can easily fulfill their needs with the help of loans. Loan is a thing which may lead to quarrels and fights if the repayment is not done on time and hence karz-e-hasna has been given more importance. Detailed information is given in the Holy Quran and Sahih Hadith so that this noble deed does not lead to disputes.\n2. While the giving of a loan has been termed a noble deed having many benefits, the act of not repaying a loan has been termed a great sin. According to a sahih hadith, the soul of a momin who does not repay a loan is trapped between the earth and the sky till it is repaid. (Tirmizi, 1078 and Ibn-Maaja, 2413)\nThere are many supplications attributed to the Holy Prophet(saws). One of them is:\n“O Allah(swt)! Relieve us of our debts and save us from poverty.”\n(Muslim, 2713)\nAccording to another sahih hadith:\n“The sins of the one who is killed in the path of Allah(swt) are wiped away except kharz.”\n(Muslim, 1886)\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) would refuse to lead the funeral prayers of a person who dies without repaying his loans. (See Bukhari, 2298 and Muslim, 1719). But in case of somebody taking the responsibility of repaying the loans, he(saws) would lead the prayers because not repaying a loan is tantamount to an act of injustice towards the person who gives the loan as he is prevented from giving further loans and the poor and needy are the ultimate sufferers. For recovering the loan, the creditor is allowed to be a little harsh. But the Holy Prophet(saws) advised softness because maybe the debtor is unable to repay the loan due to some genuine difficulty. It is narrated in one sahih hadith that Ibn-Abi-Hadrad had taken a loan from Kaab-bin-Maalik. Due to a dispute, their voices were raised in the mosque. The Holy Prophet(saws) raised the curtain of his door and told Kaab-bin-Maalik, “O Kaab, pardon half the debt.” Kaab immediately accepted the verdict. Then the Holy Prophet(saws) told Ibn-Abi-Hadrad, “Go return half the loan.” (Bukhari, 457 and Muslim, 1558).\nIt is also narrated in one sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Allah(swt) is merciful to one who is soft in matters of selling, buying and returning of loans.” (Bukhari, 2076)\nThere are many other hadith which undisputedly prove that Allah(swt) sent the Holy Prophet(saws) as ‘Rahmatullil-aalameen’ that is, as ‘mercy to mankind.’\nSo, it is desirable that if the debtor is unable to repay the full loan amount, the creditor pardons some amount because generally the creditor is richer than the debtor and it is the duty of the debtor that he tries to repay the loan as soon as possible.\nA society which is based on such excellent and noble principles will definitely be an example to the entire world and this is what Islam teaches us."],[182,"§Khazaf\nKhazaf means to pelt stones that is, to slander. In Islamic terminology Khazaf means to slander a woman or accuse her of immoral conduct. The accusation may be true or false.\nFalsely accusing a woman is one of the seven major sins. The Holy Prophet(saws) has said that the seven major sins are as follows:\n“Ascribing partners to Allah(swt), practicing magic, killing somebody, taking interest, eating the wealth of an orphan, running away from a battle and slandering chaste believing women.”\n(Bukhari, 2766 and Muslim, 8)\nإِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَرْمُونَ الْمُحْصَنَاتِ الْغَافِلَاتِ الْمُؤْمِنَاتِ لُعِنُوا فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ\nThose who slander chaste women, indiscreet but believing, are cursed in this life and in the Hereafter: for them is a grievous Penalty,-\n(Quran, Surah-24, An-Noor, Verse-23)\nAccusing somebody falsely is forbidden as is accusing somebody without ample proof. But in some cases, Khazaf becomes not only right but compulsory. For example if a man sees his wife committing adultery and is certain that the child born thereafter is not his, then it is compulsory for him to state the facts else the child will be considered his own which is not the case.\nIn some cases, Khazaf is permissible but not compulsory. For example if a man finds his wife cheating on him but is not certain if the child born thereafter is his or not, then Khazaf is permissible but not compulsory.\nPunishment for the one who commits Khazaf:\nPunishment for a slanderer is described in the Holy Quran as:\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ يَرْمُونَ الْمُحْصَنَاتِ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَأْتُوا بِأَرْبَعَةِ شُهَدَاءَ فَاجْلِدُوهُمْ ثَمَانِينَ جَلْدَةً وَلَا تَقْبَلُوا لَهُمْ شَهَادَةً أَبَدًا ۚ وَأُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْفَاسِقُونَ ٤ إِلَّا الَّذِينَ تَابُوا مِن بَعْدِ ذَٰلِكَ وَأَصْلَحُوا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ ٥﴾\nAnd those who launch a charge against chaste women, and produce not four witnesses (to support their allegations),- flog them with eighty stripes; and reject their evidence ever after: for such men are wicked transgressors;- Unless they repent thereafter and mend (their conduct); for Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.\n(Quran, Surah-24, An-Noor, Verses-4-5)\nThree types of punishment have been prescribed for the slanderer:\n1. The one who accuses falsely is to be flogged eighty times.\n2. His evidence will not be accepted in future.\n3. He will always be considered a transgressor.\nBut if the slanderer repents and seeks forgiveness; that is, if he declares that whatever he has said is false, then his testimony may be accepted in future. But he cannot escape the first punishment. But for this it is necessary that the accused person seeks it from the court. But if the slanderer is the husband of the woman, the rules are different (For this see: ‘Liyaan’)\nWhen we study the rules pertaining to slander, we understand that Islam seeks to establish a healthy society in which people do not accuse each other baselessly because Islam emphasizes the sanctity of human life, human wealth, human dignity and human chastity. That is why a person who violates these needs to be punished in such a way that it becomes a deterrent to others."],[183,"§Khizr\nKhizr is the name of a slave and devotee of Allah(swt) about whom it is said that wherever he sat, the ground became green with vegetation. (See Bukhari, 3402)\nThat is why he came to be known as ‘Khizr’ which means ‘green colour’. He is not mentioned by name in the Holy Quran, but the person who is described in the story of Musa(as) in the surah Al-Kahf has been referred to as ‘Khizr’ in the sahih hadith. Let us look at the description given in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِفَتَاهُ لَا أَبْرَحُ حَتَّىٰ أَبْلُغَ مَجْمَعَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ أَوْ أَمْضِيَ حُقُبًا ٦٠ فَلَمَّا بَلَغَا مَجْمَعَ بَيْنِهِمَا نَسِيَا حُوتَهُمَا فَاتَّخَذَ سَبِيلَهُ فِي الْبَحْرِ سَرَبًا ٦١ فَلَمَّا جَاوَزَا قَالَ لِفَتَاهُ آتِنَا غَدَاءَنَا لَقَدْ لَقِينَا مِن سَفَرِنَا هَٰذَا نَصَبًا ٦٢ قَالَ أَرَأَيْتَ إِذْ أَوَيْنَا إِلَى الصَّخْرَةِ فَإِنِّي نَسِيتُ الْحُوتَ وَمَا أَنسَانِيهُ إِلَّا الشَّيْطَانُ أَنْ أَذْكُرَهُ ۚ وَاتَّخَذَ سَبِيلَهُ فِي الْبَحْرِ عَجَبًا ٦٣ قَالَ ذَٰلِكَ مَا كُنَّا نَبْغِ ۚ فَارْتَدَّا عَلَىٰ آثَارِهِمَا قَصَصًا ٦٤ فَوَجَدَا عَبْدًا مِّنْ عِبَادِنَا آتَيْنَاهُ رَحْمَةً مِّنْ عِندِنَا وَعَلَّمْنَاهُ مِن لَّدُنَّا عِلْمًا ٦٥ قَالَ لَهُ مُوسَىٰ هَلْ أَتَّبِعُكَ عَلَىٰ أَن تُعَلِّمَنِ مِمَّا عُلِّمْتَ رُشْدًا ٦٦ قَالَ إِنَّكَ لَن تَسْتَطِيعَ مَعِيَ صَبْرًا ٦٧ وَكَيْفَ تَصْبِرُ عَلَىٰ مَا لَمْ تُحِطْ بِهِ خُبْرًا ٦٨ قَالَ سَتَجِدُنِي إِن شَاءَ اللَّهُ صَابِرًا وَلَا أَعْصِي لَكَ أَمْرًا ٦٩ قَالَ فَإِنِ اتَّبَعْتَنِي فَلَا تَسْأَلْنِي عَن شَيْءٍ حَتَّىٰ أُحْدِثَ لَكَ مِنْهُ ذِكْرًا ٧٠ فَانطَلَقَا حَتَّىٰ إِذَا رَكِبَا فِي السَّفِينَةِ خَرَقَهَا ۖ قَالَ أَخَرَقْتَهَا لِتُغْرِقَ أَهْلَهَا لَقَدْ جِئْتَ شَيْئًا إِمْرًا ٧١ قَالَ أَلَمْ أَقُلْ إِنَّكَ لَن تَسْتَطِيعَ مَعِيَ صَبْرًا ٧٢ قَالَ لَا تُؤَاخِذْنِي بِمَا نَسِيتُ وَلَا تُرْهِقْنِي مِنْ أَمْرِي عُسْرًا ٧٣ فَانطَلَقَا حَتَّىٰ إِذَا لَقِيَا غُلَامًا فَقَتَلَهُ قَالَ أَقَتَلْتَ نَفْسًا زَكِيَّةً بِغَيْرِ نَفْسٍ لَّقَدْ جِئْتَ شَيْئًا نُّكْرًا ٧٤ (16) ۞ قَالَ أَلَمْ أَقُل لَّكَ إِنَّكَ لَن تَسْتَطِيعَ مَعِيَ صَبْرًا ٧٥ قَالَ إِن سَأَلْتُكَ عَن شَيْءٍ بَعْدَهَا فَلَا تُصَاحِبْنِي ۖ قَدْ بَلَغْتَ مِن لَّدُنِّي عُذْرًا ٧٦ فَانطَلَقَا حَتَّىٰ إِذَا أَتَيَا أَهْلَ قَرْيَةٍ اسْتَطْعَمَا أَهْلَهَا فَأَبَوْا أَن يُضَيِّفُوهُمَا فَوَجَدَا فِيهَا جِدَارًا يُرِيدُ أَن يَنقَضَّ فَأَقَامَهُ ۖ قَالَ لَوْ شِئْتَ لَاتَّخَذْتَ عَلَيْهِ أَجْرًا ٧٧ قَالَ هَٰذَا فِرَاقُ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنِكَ ۚ سَأُنَبِّئُكَ بِتَأْوِيلِ مَا لَمْ تَسْتَطِع عَّلَيْهِ صَبْرًا ٧٨ أَمَّا السَّفِينَةُ فَكَانَتْ لِمَسَاكِينَ يَعْمَلُونَ فِي الْبَحْرِ فَأَرَدتُّ أَنْ أَعِيبَهَا وَكَانَ وَرَاءَهُم مَّلِكٌ يَأْخُذُ كُلَّ سَفِينَةٍ غَصْبًا ٧٩ وَأَمَّا الْغُلَامُ فَكَانَ أَبَوَاهُ مُؤْمِنَيْنِ فَخَشِينَا أَن يُرْهِقَهُمَا طُغْيَانًا وَكُفْرًا ٨٠ فَأَرَدْنَا أَن يُبْدِلَهُمَا رَبُّهُمَا خَيْرًا مِّنْهُ زَكَاةً وَأَقْرَبَ رُحْمًا ٨١ وَأَمَّا الْجِدَارُ فَكَانَ لِغُلَامَيْنِ يَتِيمَيْنِ فِي الْمَدِينَةِ وَكَانَ تَحْتَهُ كَنزٌ لَّهُمَا وَكَانَ أَبُوهُمَا صَالِحًا فَأَرَادَ رَبُّكَ أَن يَبْلُغَا أَشُدَّهُمَا وَيَسْتَخْرِجَا كَنزَهُمَا رَحْمَةً مِّن رَّبِّكَ ۚ وَمَا فَعَلْتُهُ عَنْ أَمْرِي ۚ ذَٰلِكَ تَأْوِيلُ مَا لَمْ تَسْطِع عَّلَيْهِ صَبْرًا ٨٢﴾\nBehold, Moses said to his attendant, \"I will not give up until I reach the junction of the two seas or (until) I spend years and years in travel.\" But when they reached the Junction, they forgot (about) their Fish, which took its course through the sea (straight) as in a tunnel. When they had passed on (some distance), Moses said to his attendant: \"Bring us our early meal; truly we have suffered much fatigue at this (stage of) our journey.\" He replied: \"Sawest thou (what happened) when we betook ourselves to the rock? I did indeed forget (about) the Fish: none but Satan made me forget to tell (you) about it: it took its course through the sea in a marvellous way!\" Moses said: \"That was what we were seeking after:\" So they went back on their footsteps, following (the path they had come). So they found one of Our servants, on whom We had bestowed Mercy from Ourselves and whom We had taught knowledge from Our own Presence. Moses said to him: \"May I follow thee, on the footing that thou teach me something of the (Higher) Truth which thou hast been taught?\" (The other) said: \"Verily thou wilt not be able to have patience with me!\" \"And how canst thou have patience about things about which thy understanding is not complete?\" Moses said: \"Thou wilt find me, if Allah so will, (truly) patient: nor shall I disobey thee in aught.\" The other said: \"If then thou wouldst follow me, ask me no questions about anything until I myself speak to thee concerning it.\"\nSo they both proceeded: until, when they were in the boat, he scuttled it. Said Moses: \"Hast thou scuttled it in order to drown those in it? Truly a strange thing hast thou done!\" He answered: \"Did I not tell thee that thou canst have no patience with me?\" Moses said: \"Rebuke me not for forgetting, nor grieve me by raising difficulties in my case.\" Then they proceeded: until, when they met a young man, he slew him. Moses said: \"Hast thou slain an innocent person who had slain none? Truly a foul (unheard of) thing hast thou done!\" He answered: \"Did I not tell thee that thou canst have no patience with me?\" (Moses) said: \"If ever I ask thee about anything after this, keep me not in thy company: then wouldst thou have received (full) excuse from my side.\" Then they proceeded: until, when they came to the inhabitants of a town, they asked them for food, but they refused them hospitality. They found there a wall on the point of falling down, but he set it up straight. (Moses) said: \"If thou hadst wished, surely thou couldst have exacted some recompense for it!\" He answered: \"This is the parting between me and thee: now will I tell thee the interpretation of (those things) over which thou wast unable to hold patience. \"As for the boat, it belonged to certain men in dire want: they plied on the water: I but wished to render it unserviceable, for there was after them a certain king who seized on every boat by force. \"As for the youth, his parents were people of Faith, and we feared that he would grieve them by obstinate rebellion and ingratitude (to Allah and man). \"So we desired that their Lord would give them in exchange (a son) better in purity (of conduct) and closer in affection. \"As for the wall, it belonged to two youths, orphans, in the Town; there was, beneath it, a buried treasure, to which they were entitled: their father had been a righteous man: So thy Lord desired that they should attain their age of full strength and get out their treasure - a mercy (and favour) from thy Lord. I did it not of my own accord. Such is the interpretation of (those things) over which thou wast unable to hold patience.\"\n(Quran, Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verses-60-82)\nIt is narrated in sahih Bukhari that once when Musa(as) stood up to address the Bani-Israel, a person asked him, “Do you know somebody who is wiser than you?” Musa(as) replied, “No.” When Allah(swt) informed him through a revelation, Musa(as) expressed his desire to meet him. Allah(swt) made the fish a sign and informed him that at the place where the fish would go into the sea, he would find His(swt) servant and that is what happened as is described in the Holy Quran. (See Sahih Bukhari, 74)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that when Musa(as) met Khizr, he requested Khizr to teach him whatever had been taught to him. Khizr replied, “You will not be able to stay with me, O Musa! I do not have the knowledge which Allah(swt) has given you and you do not have the knowledge which Allah(swt) has given me.” Then both of them got into a boat. They saw a small bird peck at the water in the ocean and collect a drop in its beak. Khizr then said to Musa(as), “O Musa(as)! The knowledge which you and I possess is as insignificant as the drop of water collected by that bird when compared to the knowledge of Allah(swt).”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 4725)\nBriefly it can be said that Allah(swt) gave Khizr the mystic or hidden knowledge while Musa(as) was given practical knowledge of the Shariah because that was what was necessary for the guidance of Bani-Israel and the hidden knowledge of Khizr was to prove to Musa(as) that for every wise person there is somebody wiser than him and ultimately the wisest is Allah(swt).(See: Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-76)\nOur knowledge concerning Khizr is also limited. As to what is said in the historical books and commentaries, they are unreliable. Our belief is that he was a slave of Allah(swt), he was neither an angel nor a prophet, neither is he still alive nor will he be alive till Doomsday, but has died according to the rules of Allah(swt). And the task for which he was sent has been accomplished and there is no further need for him to be in existence. The Holy Quran says:\nوَمَا جَعَلْنَا لِبَشَرٍ مِّن قَبْلِكَ الْخُلْدَ ۖ أَفَإِن مِّتَّ فَهُمُ الْخَالِدُونَ\nWe granted not to any man before thee permanent life (here): if then thou shouldst die, would they live permanently?\n(Quran, Surah-21, Al-Anbiya, Verse-34)"],[184,"§Kitab\nThe common meaning of this word is ‘a book’; but in the Holy Quran this word has been used in various contexts:\nReligious book: For example the Holy Quran has been called ‘The Book’ in verse-1 of surah-2, Al-Baqara:\nذَٰلِكَ الْكِتَابُ لَا رَيْبَ ۛ فِيهِ ۛ هُدًى لِّلْمُتَّقِينَ\nThis is the Book; in it is guidance sure, without doubt, to those who fear Allah;\nThat is, there is no doubt that this book is from Allah(swt).\nهُوَ الَّذِي أَنزَلَ عَلَيْكَ الْكِتَابَ\nHe it is Who has sent down to thee the Book.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Aal-i-Imran, Verse-7)\nIn the same way, the holy books which were revealed before the Holy Quran are also called ‘books’.\nThe Holy Quran says with respect to the Taurah:\nوَإِذْ آتَيْنَا مُوسَى الْكِتَابَ وَالْفُرْقَانَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ\nAnd remember We gave Moses the Scripture and the Criterion (Between right and wrong): There was a chance for you to be guided aright.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-53)\nIn the same way Injeel is also called ‘the book’ in the Holy Quran:\nقَالَ إِنِّي عَبْدُ اللَّهِ آتَانِيَ الْكِتَابَ وَجَعَلَنِي نَبِيًّا\nHe said: \"I am indeed a servant of Allah: He hath given me revelation and made me a prophet;\n(Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verse-30)\nLauhe-Mahfooz: This is a record where all the destinies of all creatures are stored and whatever has happened, whatever is happening and whatever will happen is recorded.\nEven this book is called ‘the book’ in the Holy Quran:\nوَمَا مِن دَابَّةٍ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلَا طَائِرٍ يَطِيرُ بِجَنَاحَيْهِ إِلَّا أُمَمٌ أَمْثَالُكُم ۚ مَّا فَرَّطْنَا فِي الْكِتَابِ مِن شَيْءٍ ۚ ثُمَّ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِمْ يُحْشَرُونَ\nThere is not an animal (that lives) on the earth, nor a being that flies on its wings, but (forms part of) communities like you. Nothing have we omitted from the Book, and they (all) shall be gathered to their Lord in the end.\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’aam, Verse-38)\nوَمَا يَعْزُبُ عَن رَّبِّكَ مِن مِّثْقَالِ ذَرَّةٍ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلَا فِي السَّمَاءِ وَلَا أَصْغَرَ مِن ذَٰلِكَ وَلَا أَكْبَرَ إِلَّا فِي كِتَابٍ مُّبِينٍ\nNor is hidden from thy Lord (so much as) the weight of an atom on the earth or in heaven. And not the least and not the greatest of these things but are recorded in a clear record.\n(Quran, Surah-10, Yunus, Verse-61)\nوَمَا مِن دَابَّةٍ فِي الْأَرْضِ إِلَّا عَلَى اللَّهِ رِزْقُهَا وَيَعْلَمُ مُسْتَقَرَّهَا وَمُسْتَوْدَعَهَا ۚ كُلٌّ فِي كِتَابٍ مُّبِينٍ\nThere is no moving creature on earth but its sustenance dependeth on Allah: He knoweth the time and place of its definite abode and its temporary deposit: All is in a clear Record.\n(Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verse-6)\nوَمَا مِنْ غَائِبَةٍ فِي السَّمَاءِ وَالْأَرْضِ إِلَّا فِي كِتَابٍ مُّبِينٍ\nNor is there aught of the unseen, in heaven or earth, but is (recorded) in a clear record.\n(Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-75)\nBook of deeds: Every person will be given his book of deeds. The word ‘the book’ is used for this also in the Holy Quran:\n﴿كَلَّا إِنَّ كِتَابَ الْفُجَّارِ لَفِي سِجِّينٍ ٧ وَمَا أَدْرَاكَ مَا سِجِّينٌ ٨ كِتَابٌ مَّرْقُومٌ ٩﴾\nNay! Surely the record of the wicked is (preserved) in Sijjin. And what will explain to thee what Sijjin is? (There is) a Register (fully) inscribed.\n(Quran, Surah-83, Al-Mutaffifin, Verses-7-9)\nThat is, Sijjin is a place where the record of the sins of the sinners is maintained. It says at one place in the Holy Quran:\nوَأَمَّا مَنْ أُوتِيَ كِتَابَهُ بِشِمَالِهِ فَيَقُولُ يَا لَيْتَنِي لَمْ أُوتَ كِتَابِيَهْ\nAnd he that will be given his Record in his left hand, will say: \"Ah! Would that my Record had not been given to me!\n(Quran, Surah-69, Al-Haaqqa, Verse-25)\nThe pious will say:\nفَأَمَّا مَنْ أُوتِيَ كِتَابَهُ بِيَمِينِهِ فَيَقُولُ هَاؤُمُ اقْرَءُوا كِتَابِيَهْ\nThen he that will be given his Record in his right hand will say: \"Ah here! Read ye my Record!\n(Quran, Surah-69, Al-Haaqqa, Verse-19)\nNormal letter: For example when Sulaiman(as) gave the bird hudhud the letter to be taken to the queen of Sheba:\n﴿اذْهَب بِّكِتَابِي هَٰذَا فَأَلْقِهْ إِلَيْهِمْ ثُمَّ تَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ فَانظُرْ مَاذَا يَرْجِعُونَ ٢٨ قَالَتْ يَا أَيُّهَا الْمَلَأُ إِنِّي أُلْقِيَ إِلَيَّ كِتَابٌ كَرِيمٌ ٢٩ إِنَّهُ مِن سُلَيْمَانَ وَإِنَّهُ بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ ٣٠﴾\n\"Go thou, with this letter of mine, and deliver it to them: then draw back from them, and (wait to) see what answer they return\"... (The queen) said: \"Ye chiefs! here is delivered to me - a letter worthy of respect.\"It is from Solomon, and is (as follows): 'In the name of Allah, Most Gracious, Most Merciful:\n(Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verses-28-30)\nWhat has been ordained. The Holy Quran says:\nلَّوْلَا كِتَابٌ مِّنَ اللَّهِ سَبَقَ لَمَسَّكُمْ فِيمَا أَخَذْتُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ\nHad it not been for a previous ordainment from Allah, a severe penalty would have reached you for the (ransom) that ye took.\n(Quran, Surah-8, Al-Anfaal, Verse-68)\nHere the reference is to the battle of Badr in which the Muslims were victorious. They would free the war-prisoners after taking the ransom while what was required was that first the enemy should be weakened to such a state that they would not be able to attack the Muslims again. But because this was allowed, Allah(swt) forgave them as is mentioned in the next verse. In this verse ‘the book’ means the decision of Allah(swt) which He(swt) had ordained previously."],[185,"§Knowledge and Science\nSome people are of the opinion that religion and scientific knowledge cannot co-exist. In their opinion religion is based on belief and myth and the light of science can wreak havoc as far as blind beliefs and superstitions are concerned and therefore religious scholars have opposed the acquiring of scientific knowledge. This is the reason why the pope started feeling insecure about Christianity when there was scientific progress in Europe and started criticizing the scientists. So much so that scores of scientists were hanged and the results of their wonderful research were thrown into the fire. This gave rise to the misconception that science and religion cannot go hand in hand and this notion is being propagated even today.\nActually when we study the origin of different religions, we come to know that many of them are based on myth and superstitions and the commentaries are based on imaginary things. When we try to prove them with the help of science, we find a vast difference between science and religion. This is because the scientists of today do not believe the ancient imaginary stories. These modern practical minded people no longer believe in the imaginary historical heroes. The religious rituals no longer hold any charm for them and they appear bored of all the pujas and prayers. This attitude of theirs has made them rebels in their religion.\nThis is the distorted notion of religion in the twenty first century. Maybe it is the ultimate goal of man to see the future based on scientific knowledge beyond the constraints of space and time. Living on this earth, man wants to travel the skies. He has managed to trample on the beauty of the moon. In today’s scientific age, some people consider religion as nothing but a bundle of superstitions due to which a distorted form of religion exists in the minds of many.\nKeeping aside the other religions we shall concentrate on Islam and its teachings which lay great stress on acquiring knowledge. Islam does not give any importance to belief without knowledge. While reading this we should imagine the conditions prevalent more than fourteen hundred years ago and then we can easily understand that Islam is based on truth and sound scientific knowledge because it advocates the acquisition of knowledge even in the days when knowledge was not given any importance at all. Life was just about eating and drinking and blindly believing in some false deities.\nThe very first verse which was revealed to the Holy Prophet(saws) was:\n﴿اقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ ١ خَلَقَ الْإِنسَانَ مِنْ عَلَقٍ ٢ اقْرَأْ وَرَبُّكَ الْأَكْرَمُ ٣ الَّذِي عَلَّمَ بِالْقَلَمِ ٤ عَلَّمَ الْإِنسَانَ مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْ ٥﴾\nRecite in the name of your Lord who created - Created man from a clinging substance. Recite, and your Lord is the most Generous - Who taught by the pen - Taught man that which he knew not.\n(Quran, Surah-96, Al-Alaq, Verses-1-5)\nWhen we study the above verses we come to know how much stress Islam lays on knowledge. The very first injunction was to read and acquire knowledge and a religion which is based on these principles at the very outset can only boast of a sound future based on truth and knowledge.\nIn the following sections the scientific aspect of the Holy Quran is highlighted. The Holy Quran is a miracle which will continue to astound the reader how many ever times he reads it.\nEncouragement to gain knowledge:\nThe Holy Quran says:\nوَمَا كَانَ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ لِيَنفِرُوا كَافَّةً ۚ فَلَوْلَا نَفَرَ مِن كُلِّ فِرْقَةٍ مِّنْهُمْ طَائِفَةٌ لِّيَتَفَقَّهُوا فِي الدِّينِ وَلِيُنذِرُوا قَوْمَهُمْ إِذَا رَجَعُوا إِلَيْهِمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَحْذَرُونَ\nAnd it is not for the believers to go forth [to battle] all at once. For there should separate from every division of them a group [remaining] to obtain understanding in the religion and warn their people when they return to them that they might be cautious.\n(Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-122)\nThis one verse from the Holy Quran is enough to disprove all the misconceptions spread by the disbelievers that Islam is against knowledge and hence progress. If it had been so, it would not ask the people to come out of their homes and seek knowledge in order to warn people about the difference between truth and falsehood, good and evil, justice and injustice etc.\nToday there is violence and aggression everywhere while man is dreaming about the skies. But the peace for which he has pawned everything still eludes him. This is because he has forsaken the one true path and has taken up other ones and has gone astray. The main aim of scientific knowledge was to create a comfortable and peaceful society but instead man is misusing his power in creating atom bombs and is bent on the destruction of human existence itself. Islam was never against obtaining knowledge which makes man a true human being.\nIt may be surprising to some that the Holy Quran addresses the Holy Prophet(saws) as:\nفَاعْلَمْ أَنَّهُ لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لِذَنبِكَ وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ\nSo know, [O Muhammad], that there is no deity except Allah and ask forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and believing women.\n(Quran, Surah-47, Muhammad, Verse-19)\nHere it is being made clear that until and unless the worshipper knows that the only One worthy of worship is Allah(swt), his worship will not be true and complete. In other words we can say that he should gain complete understanding so that the person does not go astray and start praying someone else.\nThis is also a warning for those who consider religion to be a school of thought which is based mainly on superstitions and so not take the trouble of trying to understand the true religion. Their opinion may be true regarding other religions but as far as Islam is concerned they are thoroughly mistaken.\nTo further elucidate the above a few teachings of the Holy Prophet(saws) are being mentioned here.\nIt is narrated by Qais-bin-Qaseer that he was once seated with Abu-Darda in a mosque in Damascus when a man came up and said, “O Abu-Darda! I have come to you from Madina because I heard that you narrate the hadith of the Holy Prophet(saws).”\nAbu-Darda narrated that he heard the Holy Prophet(saws) say:\n“The person who goes forth in search of knowledge, the angels spread their wings in his path and Allah(swt) makes his path easy.”\n(Ibn-Majah 226)\nAnas narrates that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“The person who sets out in search of knowledge is on the path of Allah(swt) till he returns.”\n(Tirmizi 2647)\nAbdullah-bin-Abbas narrates that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“The person whom Allah(swt) decides to favour, He(swt) will give an understanding of religion.”\nAbu-Darda says that the advice of the Holy Prophet(saws) was:\n“The superiority of the learned man over the devout is like that of the moon, on the night when it is full, over the rest of the stars. The learned are the heirs of the Prophets, and the Prophets leave neither dinar nor dirham, leaving only knowledge, and he who takes it takes an abundant portion.”\n(Abu Dawood 3641 and Ibn-Majah 223)\nAbu Huraira narrates that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n\"The word of wisdom is [like] the lost property of a wise man. So wherever he finds it, he is entitled to it.\"\n(Tirmizi)\nThese were a few hadith which stressed the need for acquiring knowledge. Now let us look at a few which condemn the hiding of knowledge and prevent it from being spread. This will prove that Islam is a scientific religion which lays great stress on knowledge, both seeking it and also spreading it.\nCriticising a person who hides knowledge:\nEducation and learning are very important aspects of Islam and that is why the Holy Quran severely criticises the people who hide knowledge from others and do not strive to spread it so that others may also benefit from it. Now let us look at some verses of the Holy Quran which speak against the person who hides the knowledge and truth:\nوَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّن كَتَمَ شَهَادَةً عِندَهُ مِنَ اللَّهِ\nAnd who is more unjust than one who conceals a testimony he has from Allah?\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-140)\nBy ‘testimony’ here what is meant according to the Islamic religious scholars is the Jews and the Christians hiding the fact about the coming of Muhammad(saws) which was revealed in their religious books. And when Muhammad(saws) himself declared his prophethood, they refused to believe him. In the Hindu scriptures, the Vedas and the Puranas also the coming of the prophet Muhammad(saws) has been mentioned. Let us look at a few instances:\n“In another country a spiritual leader is going to come with his companions whose name will be Mahamad and he will come in the desert land.”\n(Bhavishya Purana 323 s.5/8)\nWe clearly understand the name and the region from this shlok and sutra. The other qualities of the person who was to come are expressed as under:\n“He will be circumcised at birth, he will not have matted hair, he will have a beard, he will eat meat, he will declare his message clearly and in a strong language, and the people believing in his message will be called muslayi.”\nStudy the above shlok carefully. Circumcision was not a Hindu custom. Matted hair was the sign of ascetics and religious leaders. The great leader who was to come, that is Muhammad(saws) possessed all these qualities. And the people believing his message will be called Muslayi. This word points to the word ‘Musalman’.\nThe shlok from Atharvaved part 20 says:\n“O people! Listen carefully, the praised one, the praised one mahamahe great rishi will come among sixty thousand and ninety nine people.”\nMuhammad means ‘the one who is praised’. When Muhammad(saws) was born the population of Makka was sixty thousand.\nThe Holy Quran calls Muhammad(saws) a ‘mercy for the entire world’. It says in the Rigveda:\n“The one with the name mercy, the praised one will come with ten thousand companions.”\n(Mantra 5/27/1)\nIn this way in the vedas, Mahamahe and Mahamad are the words used to mention the coming of the prophet Muhammad(saws). This meaning is fine but we should go into further detail and include every piece of evidence and testimony be it in the form of teaching or knowledge about something which is useful for mankind. The Holy Quran says:\nوَلَا تَلْبِسُوا الْحَقَّ بِالْبَاطِلِ وَتَكْتُمُوا الْحَقَّ وَأَنتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ\nAnd do not mix the truth with falsehood or conceal the truth while you know [it].\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-42)\nمَّا عَلَى الرَّسُولِ إِلَّا الْبَلَاغُ ۗ وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تُبْدُونَ وَمَا تَكْتُمُونَ\nNot upon the Messenger is [responsibility] except [for] notification. And Allah knows whatever you reveal and whatever you conceal.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-99)\nوَإِذْ أَخَذَ اللَّهُ مِيثَاقَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ لَتُبَيِّنُنَّهُ لِلنَّاسِ وَلَا تَكْتُمُونَهُ فَنَبَذُوهُ وَرَاءَ ظُهُورِهِمْ وَاشْتَرَوْا بِهِ ثَمَنًا قَلِيلًا ۖ فَبِئْسَ مَا يَشْتَرُونَ\nAnd [mention, O Muhammad], when Allah took a covenant from those who were given the Scripture, [saying], \"You must make it clear to the people and not conceal it.\" But they threw it away behind their backs and exchanged it for a small price. And wretched is that which they purchased.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-187)\nIt is clear from the above verse that the previous tribes concealed the knowledge revealed to them by Allah(swt) and did not spread it among the people. This is a great injustice and sin because these previous scriptures were also a treasure-house of knowledge like the Holy Quran and the one who does not reveal them is a great sinner and disbeliever. The Holy Quran says:\nإِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَكْتُمُونَ مَا أَنزَلْنَا مِنَ الْبَيِّنَاتِ وَالْهُدَىٰ مِن بَعْدِ مَا بَيَّنَّاهُ لِلنَّاسِ فِي الْكِتَابِ ۙ أُولَٰئِكَ يَلْعَنُهُمُ اللَّهُ وَيَلْعَنُهُمُ اللَّاعِنُونَ\nIndeed, those who conceal what We sent down of clear proofs and guidance after We made it clear for the people in the Scripture - those are cursed by Allah and cursed by those who curse.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-159)\nإِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَكْتُمُونَ مَا أَنزَلَ اللَّهُ مِنَ الْكِتَابِ وَيَشْتَرُونَ بِهِ ثَمَنًا قَلِيلًا ۙ أُولَٰئِكَ مَا يَأْكُلُونَ فِي بُطُونِهِمْ إِلَّا النَّارَ وَلَا يُكَلِّمُهُمُ اللَّهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَلَا يُزَكِّيهِمْ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ\nIndeed, they who conceal what Allah has sent down of the Book and exchange it for a small price - those consume not into their bellies except the Fire. And Allah will not speak to them on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them. And they will have a painful punishment.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-174)\nThese are a few verses which warn the people who conceal the truth and make it abundantly clear that knowledge is of utmost importance in Islam. Now let us clarify it further in the light of the hadith of the Holy Prophet(saws). It is narrated by Abu Huraira that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“He who is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Judgement with a bridle of Fire.”\n(Abu-Dawood 3658, Tirmizi 2649, Ibn-Majah 261)\nIn this hadith those people have been warned who possess knowledge but do not pass it on to others as a result of which it remains limited to a few people. Others do not benefit from it and the benefits of knowledge are greatly reduced. It is also possible that the person seeking knowledge may be more discerning and hence reap greater benefits from it as is narrated in another sahih hadith:\nAbdullah-bin-Masood narrates that he heard the Holy Prophet(saws) say:\n“May Allah(swt) keep that person happy who has heard my word, remembered it and conveyed it to the people in its correct form. Because it is often the case that the person conveying a wise and knowledgeable word is very wise or knowledgeable and it is also possible that the person to whom the word is conveyed is more wise than the person conveying it.”\n(Tirmizi 2658 and Ibn-Majah 232)\nThis hadith says that the wise people should not hide their knowledge and wisdom. This harms the entire society because the bearer often does not understand the importance of what he possesses. So, if he passes it on to others, he may benefit from it in his own way because everybody does not have the wisdom and understanding to use it for the good of the society.\nSo, in this hadith, in a way those people are being criticized who hide their knowledge.\nAnd care should also be taken that the person to whom the knowledge is being imparted is perceiving it in the correct sense, else it may lead to some misinterpretation. It is narrated in one sahih hadith:\nAbdullah-bin-Masood narrates that he said:\n“When conveying some hadith, the level of understanding of the person should be considered. It is possible that you may tell him something which is beyond his understanding and it may lead to confusion.”\n(Sahih Muslim)\nThis is not a hadith of the Holy Prophet(saws) but we understand from it that we should consider the intelligence of a person while conveying words of wisdom to him.\nThe above things are with respect to Islamic teachings. In the case of teachings relevant to social life, the Holy Quran warns the people who do not make optimum use of their knowledge and common sense and compares them to animals:\nلَهُمْ قُلُوبٌ لَّا يَفْقَهُونَ بِهَا وَلَهُمْ أَعْيُنٌ لَّا يُبْصِرُونَ بِهَا وَلَهُمْ آذَانٌ لَّا يَسْمَعُونَ بِهَا ۚ أُولَٰئِكَ كَالْأَنْعَامِ بَلْ هُمْ أَضَلُّ ۚ أُولَٰئِكَ هُمُ الْغَافِلُونَ\nThey have hearts with which they do not understand, they have eyes with which they do not see, and they have ears with which they do not hear. Those are like livestock; rather, they are more astray. It is they who are the heedless.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-179)\nThis is the worst criticism of the people who have the wisdom and intelligence but do not make the effort to use it for the good of mankind and society. On the Day of Judgement, these people will own up their sin and say:\nوَقَالُوا لَوْ كُنَّا نَسْمَعُ أَوْ نَعْقِلُ مَا كُنَّا فِي أَصْحَابِ السَّعِيرِ\nAnd they will say, \"If only we had been listening or reasoning, we would not be among the companions of the Blaze.\"\n(Quran, Surah-67, Al-Mulk, Verse-10)\nTherefore Allah(swt) admonishes mankind again and again in various ways that they should see and contemplate on this vast creation and strive to maintain its harmony instead of concentrating all their energies in trying to annihilate it. So, we can declare with the utmost conviction that Islam is in favour of scientific development and unlike other religious faiths, Islam encourages and promotes science. But this does not mean that we blindly accept all the principles and theories of science. We should first test them with the basic principles of Islam and reject those which go against them.\nSumming up, we can say that the Holy Quran is a treasure-house of invaluable gems and if we set out to explain all aspects of it, all the paper and ink in this world will be exhausted but we cannot fathom the depths of it. The Holy Quran says about this:\nوَلَوْ أَنَّمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ مِن شَجَرَةٍ أَقْلَامٌ وَالْبَحْرُ يَمُدُّهُ مِن بَعْدِهِ سَبْعَةُ أَبْحُرٍ مَّا نَفِدَتْ كَلِمَاتُ اللَّهِ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ\nAnd if whatever trees upon the earth were pens and the sea [was ink], replenished thereafter by seven [more] seas, the words of Allah would not be exhausted. Indeed, Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise.\n(Quran, Surah-31, Luqman, Verse-27)"],[186,"§Knowledgeable\nAmong the many attributes of Allah(swt), ‘Aleem’ is one which can be translated as ‘knowledgeable’. This means that Allah(swt) is well aware of whatever is happening in this world. So much so that He(swt) is aware of every leaf that moves. The Holy Quran says:\nوَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ ۖ وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ اللَّهُ ۗ وَاللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ\nAnd fear Allah. And Allah teaches you. And Allah is Knowing of all things.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-282)\nAllah(swt) is aware of everything because He(swt) is the Creator of everything.\n(See: Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-101)\nIn fact Allah(swt) is even aware of what is hidden in the hearts of men. ( See: Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verse-5)\nAllah(swt) shall say to Isa(as):\nوَإِذْ قَالَ اللَّهُ يَا عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ أَأَنتَ قُلْتَ لِلنَّاسِ اتَّخِذُونِي وَأُمِّيَ إِلَٰهَيْنِ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ ۖ قَالَ سُبْحَانَكَ مَا يَكُونُ لِي أَنْ أَقُولَ مَا لَيْسَ لِي بِحَقٍّ ۚ إِن كُنتُ قُلْتُهُ فَقَدْ عَلِمْتَهُ ۚ تَعْلَمُ مَا فِي نَفْسِي وَلَا أَعْلَمُ مَا فِي نَفْسِكَ ۚ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوبِ\n\"O Jesus, Son of Mary, did you say to the people, 'Take me and my mother as deities besides Allah?'\"\nIsa(as) will reply:\n\"Exalted are You! It was not for me to say that to which I have no right. If I had said it, You would have known it. You know what is within myself, and I do not know what is within Yourself. Indeed, it is You who is Knower of the unseen.”\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-116)\nIt is mentioned again and again in the Holy Quran that Allah(swt) is ‘Most Knowledgeable’. This is one of the many beautiful attributes of Allah(swt) and it is impossible to imagine Him(swt) without it.\nThe knowledge of Allah(swt) is His own (inherent) and unlimited while the knowledge that we possess is limited and derived (something which we have gained from somewhere). That is why a new-born has no knowledge at all:\nوَاللَّهُ أَخْرَجَكُم مِّن بُطُونِ أُمَّهَاتِكُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَ شَيْئًا وَجَعَلَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْأَبْصَارَ وَالْأَفْئِدَةَ ۙ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ\nAnd Allah has extracted you from the wombs of your mothers not knowing a thing, and He made for you hearing and vision and intellect that perhaps you would be grateful.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-78)\nThat is ears, eyes and mind are the means of gaining knowledge using which man becomes knowledgeable."],[187,"§Kursi\nThe description of Kursi occurs at two places in the Holy Quran:\nFirst: In connection with Allah(swt)\nاللَّهُ لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّومُ ۚ لَا تَأْخُذُهُ سِنَةٌ وَلَا نَوْمٌ ۚ لَّهُ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ ۗ مَن ذَا الَّذِي يَشْفَعُ عِندَهُ إِلَّا بِإِذْنِهِ ۚ يَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ ۖ وَلَا يُحِيطُونَ بِشَيْءٍ مِّنْ عِلْمِهِ إِلَّا بِمَا شَاءَ ۚ وَسِعَ كُرْسِيُّهُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ ۖ وَلَا يَئُودُهُ حِفْظُهُمَا ۚ وَهُوَ الْعَلِيُّ الْعَظِيمُ\nAllah! There is no god but He,-the Living, the Self-subsisting, Eternal. No slumber can seize Him nor sleep. His are all things in the heavens and on earth. Who is there can intercede in His presence except as He permitteth? He knoweth what (appeareth to His creatures as) before or after or behind them. Nor shall they compass aught of His knowledge except as He willeth. His Throne doth extend over the heavens and the earth, and He feeleth no fatigue in guarding and preserving them for He is the Most High, the Supreme (in glory).\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-255)\nThis verse is called ‘Aayatul-Kursi’. Its importance is narrated again and again in the Sahih Hadith. According to Sahih Muslim, once the Holy Prophet(saws) asked Ubaiyy-bin-Kaab:\n“O Abu Munzir, do you know which is the great verse in the book of Allah(swt)?” He replied, “ Allah(swt) and His prophet(saws) have more knowledge.” When he(saws) asked him the same thing again, he named the verse ‘Aayatul-Kursi’. The Holy Prophet(saws) placed his hand on his heart and said,” O Abu Munzir, may Allah(swt) bless your knowledge.” (Muslim, 810)\nThere is one other hadith regarding the Aayatul Kursi. It is that when a person recites this before sleeping, an angel will be assigned to guard him the whole night and till dawn, and the satan will not come near him.( Sahih Bukhari, 2311)\nThe question arises as to what this kursi is? Is it the same ‘arsh’ which is described again and again in the Holy Quran? The scholars are of the opinion that this is something quite different, the complete knowledge about which we do not have.\nSecond: The second place where the word kursi is used is in verse 34 of surah Saad in which the kursi of Sulaiman(as) is described, seated on which he ruled his kingdom.\nوَلَقَدْ فَتَنَّا سُلَيْمَانَ وَأَلْقَيْنَا عَلَىٰ كُرْسِيِّهِ جَسَدًا ثُمَّ أَنَابَ\nAnd We did try Solomon: We placed on his throne a body (without life); but he did turn (to Us in true devotion):\n(Quran, Surah-38, Saad, Verse-34)\nWhat was this test? Which body was placed on the throne? We do not find any details about this either in the Holy Quran or in Sahih Hadith. ( For more details see : Sulaiman)"],[188,"§Laat\nThe Holy Quran mentions the names of three idols which were worshipped by the Arabs before the advent of Islam:\n﴿أَفَرَأَيْتُمُ اللَّاتَ وَالْعُزَّىٰ ١٩ وَمَنَاةَ الثَّالِثَةَ الْأُخْرَىٰ ٢٠ أَلَكُمُ الذَّكَرُ وَلَهُ الْأُنثَىٰ ٢١ تِلْكَ إِذًا قِسْمَةٌ ضِيزَىٰ ٢٢ إِنْ هِيَ إِلَّا أَسْمَاءٌ سَمَّيْتُمُوهَا أَنتُمْ وَآبَاؤُكُم مَّا أَنزَلَ اللَّهُ بِهَا مِن سُلْطَانٍ ۚ إِن يَتَّبِعُونَ إِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَمَا تَهْوَى الْأَنفُسُ ۖ وَلَقَدْ جَاءَهُم مِّن رَّبِّهِمُ الْهُدَىٰ ٢٣﴾\nSo have you considered al-Lat and al-'Uzza? And Manat, the third - the other one? Is the male for you and for Him the female? That, then, is an unjust division. They are not but [mere] names you have named them - you and your forefathers - for which Allah has sent down no authority. They follow not except assumption and what [their] souls desire, and there has already come to them from their Lord guidance.\n(Quran, Surah-53, An-Najm, Verses-19-23)\nLaat was the first of the three deities which was called the wife or daughter of God (Inna-Aoozubillah). It was in fact a white stone with various carved images on it. It was kept in a house in the city of Taif. It was decorated with a shawl and its priests would be seated all round it. This house was surrounded by open ground where the devotees would come to seek blessings and would even circumambulate the stone, like the Tawaf of the Holy Kaaba. These believers claimed superiority over all the Arabs except the Quraish.\nIt is the opinion of Yaqut Hamvi that Laat was the name of a person from Banu-Saqifa who was very brave and fearless. Upon his death people started believing that his spirit was wandering around a certain place and that it had made that place its abode. Then the people made an idol, placed it at that place and started worshipping it. In the beginning everyone was worshipping it and then it became the idol of only the tribe of Hawazin.\nAfter the triumph over Makka, the Holy Prophet(saws) ordered the removal of this idol in order to root out the disease of idol-worship."],[189,"§Lailatul-Qadr\n‘Lailatul-Qadr’ means ‘sacred night’. This is the same sacred night during which Allah (swt) brought down the Holy Quran from Lauhe-Mahfooz to Baitul-Izzat (which is on the first sky). Then from there He (swt) revealed it in bits and parts to His (swt) Prophet Muhammad (saws) over a period of 23 years.\nThe importance of this night is that the reward of praying on this one night is more than the reward of praying for one thousand months. Upon the command of Allah (swt) the angels along with Jibrail (as) descend to the earth on this night in order to carry out the commands of Allah (swt). This night lasts till dawn. (Surah-97, Al-Qadr, Verses-1-5). It has been mentioned in Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-185 that the Holy Quran was revealed in the month of Ramadan, so this night occurs in the month of Ramadan. It has been mentioned clearly in the sahih hadith that this night is one of the odd nights in the last ten days of the month of Ramadan. The exact day on which it occurs has not been mentioned so that the people strive to find it in the five odd days.\nIt is narrated in the sahih hadith that the person who prays on this night seeking its rewards, Allah (swt) wipes away all his sins. (Sahih Bukhari, 1901 and Sahih Muslim, 760)\nAisha (ra) narrates that the Holy Prophet (saws) spent the last ten nights of the month of Ramadan praying. He would even wake up the people of his household so that even they take advantage of the benefits of this night. (See Sahih Bukhari, 2024 and Sahih Muslim, 1174)\nAisha (ra) asked the Holy Prophet (saws), “O Apostle of Allah (swt)! If I get to know this night, what should I pray for?” The Holy Prophet (saws) replied:\n“Say! O Allah (swt)! You are the one who forgives and You like to forgive; so forgive me.” ( Tirmizi 3513, Ibn-Maajah 3850 and Ahmad 6:182)"],[190,"§Lavaqih\nThis word is used at one place in the Holy Quran (See: Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verse-22). This is the plural of ‘Laaqih’. The meaning is: a pregnant camel. The sense in which it is used in the Holy Quran is a big miracle. We can understand it in the light of science today.\nPlants are described many times in the Holy Quran. The astonishing fact to which the Holy Quran refers so many years back is the male and female parts of a plant which the modern scientists have understood today after centuries of research. The only thing the people of those days were aware of was the growing of date plants. Today science has proved that all the plants have pairs and winds carry the pollen from one plant to another and as a result fertilization takes place and then flowers and fruits grow forth.\nThe Holy Quran refers to this modern scientific truth very clearly:\nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ الْأَزْوَاجَ كُلَّهَا مِمَّا تُنبِتُ الْأَرْضُ وَمِنْ أَنفُسِهِمْ وَمِمَّا لَا يَعْلَمُونَ\nExalted is He who created all pairs - from what the earth grows and from themselves and from that which they do not know.\n(Quran, Surah-36, Ya-Sin, Verse-36)\nوَمِن كُلِّ الثَّمَرَاتِ جَعَلَ فِيهَا زَوْجَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ\nand from all of the fruits He made therein two mates;\n(Quran, Surah-13, Ar-Ra’d, Verse-3)\nوَأَرْسَلْنَا الرِّيَاحَ لَوَاقِحَ\nAnd We have sent the fertilizing winds.\n(Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verse-22)\nThat is winds carry the pollen from one plant to another. And when the female plant or female part receives the pollen, fertilization takes place and flowers and fruit start growing. This is a miracle upon which the Holy Quran is asking us to contemplate and believe in the Almighty Allah (swt) who is responsible for this awesome creation."],[191,"§Libaas\n‘Libaas’ or clothing is one of the favours of Allah (swt) upon mankind. He (swt) taught us to wear clothes and has put it in our nature to like being clothed. That is why when Adam(as) and his wife tasted the forbidden fruit, their condition became shameful to them and they started covering themselves with the leaves of the plants of paradise. (See Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-22 and Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verse-121).\nIt is a great favour of Allah (swt) that He showed us the ways to make clothes on earth.\nيَا بَنِي آدَمَ قَدْ أَنزَلْنَا عَلَيْكُمْ لِبَاسًا يُوَارِي سَوْآتِكُمْ وَرِيشًا\nO children of Adam, We have bestowed upon you clothing to conceal your private parts and as adornment.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-26)\nBestowing the clothes means giving the means of making clothes like the cotton which grows on earth, silkworms which give us silk and the other modern methods of making synthetic clothes. The dwellers of paradise will also be given clothes which will be of green silk. (See: Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hijr, Verse-23)\nBriefly the teachings of Islam regarding clothing are as follows:\n1. There is no specific clothing in Islam; but depending on the place and climate we can wear whatever is comfortable. But it is compulsory for a man to be covered from his navel to the knee. As for women, the whole body has to be covered except for the face, hands and feet.\n2. The dress of a man should not be below the ankle because it is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“The part of the dress below the ankle will be in hell-fire.”\n(Sahih Bukhari 5887)\n3. The clothes should not be such that they lead to pride. It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“A person who drags his clothes on the ground in pride and arrogance, on the Day of Judgment Allah (swt) will not look towards him.”\n(Sahih Bukhari 5783 and Sahih Muslim 2085)\n4. It is forbidden for men to wear silk. Regarding the dress of men, it is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Do not wear silk. One who wears silk in this world will not wear it in paradise.”\n(Sahih Bukhari 5833 and Sahih Muslim 2069)\n5. The Holy Prophet (saws) has cursed the men who dress like women and the women who dress like men. (Sahih Bukhari 5885).\n6. It is narrated in a sahih hadith that wearing white is best and the dead are also to be buried shrouded in white. (See Abu-Dawood 3878 and Tirmizi 994)\n7. Women who dress scantily will not go to paradise nor will they smell the fragrance of paradise while the fragrance of paradise can be smelt from afar.\n(See Sahih Muslim 2128)\n8. When the women go out they should draw their veil over their bosom. (See Surah-33, Al-Ahzab, Verse-59). This means that the face and head should be covered.\n9. Women should not display their adornments except in front of the people mentioned in surah-24, An-Noor, Verse-31. They are: husband, father, father-in-law, sons, sons of husband, brothers, sons of brothers, sons of sisters, women attendants or friends, their slaves, male attendants having no physical desire and children not aware of the private aspects of women. It is no sin to display their adornments in front of these people.\n10. Along with the above injunctions it is also commanded for both men and women to lower their glances and not stare at each other.\n﴿قُل لِّلْمُؤْمِنِينَ يَغُضُّوا مِنْ أَبْصَارِهِمْ وَيَحْفَظُوا فُرُوجَهُمْ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ أَزْكَىٰ لَهُمْ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّهَ خَبِيرٌ بِمَا يَصْنَعُونَ ٣٠ وَقُل لِّلْمُؤْمِنَاتِ يَغْضُضْنَ مِنْ أَبْصَارِهِنَّ وَيَحْفَظْنَ فُرُوجَهُنَّ﴾\nTell the believing men to reduce [some] of their vision and guard their private parts. That is purer for them. Indeed, Allah is Acquainted with what they do. And tell the believing women to reduce [some] of their vision and guard their private parts.\n(Quran, Surah-24, An-Nur, Verses-30-31)\n11. And if we inadvertently look at some member of the opposite gender, we should lower our gaze. (See Sahih Muslim 2159)\n12. We should not be alone with a woman who is not accompanied by her ‘mehram’ (father, brother etc.) (See Sahih Bukhari 5233 and Sahih Muslim 1341).\nSome people asked the Holy Prophet (saws) if a woman can be alone with her brother-in-law. The Holy Prophet (saws) replied, “Brother-in-law is death.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 5233 and Sahih Muslim, 2172)."],[192,"§Lion\nLion is called ‘Asad’ in Arabic. This particular word does not occur in the Holy Quran; but the word ‘Khaswarah’ occurs in surah-74, Al-Muddathir, verse-51 which says:\n﴿فَمَا لَهُمْ عَنِ التَّذْكِرَةِ مُعْرِضِينَ ٤٩ كَأَنَّهُمْ حُمُرٌ مُّسْتَنفِرَةٌ ٥٠ فَرَّتْ مِن قَسْوَرَةٍ ٥١﴾\nThen what is [the matter] with them that they are, from the reminder, turning away. As if they were alarmed donkeys. Fleeing from a lion?\n(Quran, Surah-74, Al-Muddathir, Verses-49-51)\nIn the above verses, the people who turn away from truth and tread the path of falsehood are being compared to a donkey who on seeing a lion tries to run away. But it cannot escape the lion just as the people who reject the truth cannot escape the ultimate painful punishment in the Hereafter."],[193,"§Liyaan\n‘Liyaan’ is an Islamic word whose meaning can be understood from the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ يَرْمُونَ أَزْوَاجَهُمْ وَلَمْ يَكُن لَّهُمْ شُهَدَاءُ إِلَّا أَنفُسُهُمْ فَشَهَادَةُ أَحَدِهِمْ أَرْبَعُ شَهَادَاتٍ بِاللَّهِ ۙ إِنَّهُ لَمِنَ الصَّادِقِينَ ٦ وَالْخَامِسَةُ أَنَّ لَعْنَتَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ إِن كَانَ مِنَ الْكَاذِبِينَ ٧ وَيَدْرَأُ عَنْهَا الْعَذَابَ أَن تَشْهَدَ أَرْبَعَ شَهَادَاتٍ بِاللَّهِ ۙ إِنَّهُ لَمِنَ الْكَاذِبِينَ ٨ وَالْخَامِسَةَ أَنَّ غَضَبَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهَا إِن كَانَ مِنَ الصَّادِقِينَ ٩﴾\nAnd those who accuse their wives [of adultery] and have no witnesses except themselves - then the witness of one of them [shall be] four testimonies [swearing] by Allah that indeed, he is of the truthful. And the fifth [oath will be] that the curse of Allah be upon him if he should be among the liars. But it will prevent punishment from her if she gives four testimonies [swearing] by Allah that indeed, he is of the liars. And the fifth [oath will be] that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he was of the truthful.\n(Quran, Surah-24, An-Nur, Verses-6-9)\nThe meaning of the above verses is that in the absence of four witnesses, the wife shall escape punishment; but because the husband himself has seen the wife committing adultery, he shall escape the punishment of ‘Khazaf’. But under these conditions it would be impossible for the husband and wife to stay together and therefore they should be legally separated. This is called ‘Liyaan’ in Islam because both of them deserve punishment if they are liars and one of them is definitely a liar who shall be cursed. Before and after Islam, a better ruling in this regard has not been given."],[194,"§Locusts\n‘Locusts’ are insects which are about two inches long. They have four wings, two short front wings and two longer hind wings. They have six legs, four for walking and two for leaping. They feed on the leaves of trees and flowers and leaves of the fields. They move in large swarms and after they attack a place, there is no vegetation left there. Therefore, farmers make elaborate arrangements to prevent these attacks. Locusts are described twice in the Holy Quran:\nFirst:\nThe Pharaoh and his tribe told Musa (as) that whatever signs he brought, they would not believe in him.So Allah(swt) sent many trials upon them:\nفَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الطُّوفَانَ وَالْجَرَادَ وَالْقُمَّلَ وَالضَّفَادِعَ وَالدَّمَ آيَاتٍ مُّفَصَّلَاتٍ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوا وَكَانُوا قَوْمًا مُّجْرِمِينَ\nSo We sent upon them the flood and locusts and lice and frogs and blood as distinct signs, but they were arrogant and were a criminal people.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-133)\n(For more information see Musa(as))\nSecond:\nThe condition of the disbelievers on the Day of Resurrection has been compared to that of locusts:\nخُشَّعًا أَبْصَارُهُمْ يَخْرُجُونَ مِنَ الْأَجْدَاثِ كَأَنَّهُمْ جَرَادٌ مُّنتَشِرٌ\nTheir eyes humbled, they will emerge from the graves as if they were locusts spreading.\n(Quran, Surah-54, Al-Qamar, Verse-7)\nAs the locusts feed on grass and leaves, it was allowed to eat them since the time of Musa(as). ( See Bible, Leviticus 11:22)\nThe favourite food of Yahya(as) was locusts and wild honey.( See : Matthew, 3:4)\nIt is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n“For us two dead things and two things with blood have been declared halal. The dead things are the liver and the spleen.”\n(See : Behqi, 1:254)\nFor cooking these, first the wings, legs and the head are cut off and the intestines taken out. Then they are roasted or fried in oil."],[195,"§Lut (as)\nLut(as) was the son of Haroon, the brother of Ibraheem(as). He believed in the prophethood of Ibraheem(as). While he was still in the city of Ur, his father passed away and he was brought up by his grandfather Azar, the father of Ibraheem(as). When Ibraheem(as) started spreading his message of monotheism and condemned idol-worship, people vehemently started opposing him. They tormented him in various ways and even tried killing him. But Allah(swt), the Most Beneficent and Most Merciful saved him and asked him to migrate to another place. When Ibraheem(as) migrated, Lut(as) also accompanied him. The Holy Quran says:\nفَآمَنَ لَهُ لُوطٌ ۘ وَقَالَ إِنِّي مُهَاجِرٌ إِلَىٰ رَبِّي ۖ إِنَّهُ هُوَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ\nAnd Lot believed him. [Abraham] said, \"Indeed, I will emigrate to [the service of] my Lord. Indeed, He is the Exalted in Might, the Wise.\"\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-26)\nLut(as) came to Egypt with Ibraheem(as). They amassed a huge wealth there and then came back to Palestine. As they had many goats and other animals with them, Ibraheem(as) stayed back in Habroon and sent Lut(as) for preaching and spreading the message of truth and taking care of the sheep and goats to the cities of Sadom and Gomorrah in Jordan. The people there were involved in various sinful activities. A few are described in the Holy Quran. One was homosexuality being committed by the men there. (See: Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-55)\nOne other crime was that they would rob the travellers coming there.\n(See: Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-29)\nThey would commit these crimes openly without any fear whatsoever.\nLut(as) forbade them from committing these crimes and said: ( See: Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-29)\n﴿إِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ أَخُوهُمْ لُوطٌ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ١٦١ إِنِّي لَكُمْ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٌ ١٦٢ فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ ١٦٣﴾\nWhen their brother Lot said to them, \"Will you not fear Allah? Indeed, I am to you a trustworthy messenger. So fear Allah and obey me.\n(Quran, Surah-26, Ash-Shu’ara, Verses-161-163)\nThe people there neither stopped their idol-worship nor did they stop committing other sins. On the other hand they started threatening Lut(as):\nقَالُوا لَئِن لَّمْ تَنتَهِ يَا لُوطُ لَتَكُونَنَّ مِنَ الْمُخْرَجِينَ\nThey said, \"If you do not desist, O Lot, you will surely be of those evicted.\"\n(Quran, Surah-26, Ash-Shu’ara, Verse-167)\nAt another place in the Holy Quran it says:\n﴿وَلُوطًا إِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهِ أَتَأْتُونَ الْفَاحِشَةَ وَأَنتُمْ تُبْصِرُونَ ٥٤ أَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَأْتُونَ الرِّجَالَ شَهْوَةً مِّن دُونِ النِّسَاءِ ۚ بَلْ أَنتُمْ قَوْمٌ تَجْهَلُونَ ٥٥ فَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوْمِهِ إِلَّا أَن قَالُوا أَخْرِجُوا آلَ لُوطٍ مِّن قَرْيَتِكُمْ ۖ إِنَّهُمْ أُنَاسٌ يَتَطَهَّرُونَ ٥٦﴾\nAnd [mention] Lot, when he said to his people, \"Do you commit immorality while you are seeing? Do you indeed approach men with desire instead of women? Rather, you are a people behaving ignorantly.\" But the answer of his people was not except that they said, \"Expel the family of Lot from your city. Indeed, they are people who keep themselves pure.\"\n(Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verses-54-56)\nIn fact there came a time when the tribe of Lut(as) said to him:\nائْتِنَا بِعَذَابِ اللَّهِ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ الصَّادِقِينَ\n\"Bring us the punishment of Allah, if you should be of the truthful.\"\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-29)\nAnd when the people crossed all limits, they had to face the wrath of Allah(swt):\nوَأَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِم مَّطَرًا ۖ فَسَاءَ مَطَرُ الْمُنذَرِينَ\nAnd We rained upon them a rain [of stones], and evil was the rain of those who were warned.\n(Quran, Surah-27, An-Naml, Verse-58)\nAt another place it says:\nإِنَّا مُنزِلُونَ عَلَىٰ أَهْلِ هَٰذِهِ الْقَرْيَةِ رِجْزًا مِّنَ السَّمَاءِ بِمَا كَانُوا يَفْسُقُونَ\nIndeed, We will bring down on the people of this city punishment from the sky because they have been defiantly disobedient.\"\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-34)\nThe punishment was in the form of a rain of stones of hard clay accompanied by a terrible shriek which turned the whole place topsy-turvy. ( See : Quran, Surah-15, Al-Hijr, Verses-73,74)\n﴿وَإِنَّ لُوطًا لَّمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ١٣٣ إِذْ نَجَّيْنَاهُ وَأَهْلَهُ أَجْمَعِينَ ١٣٤ إِلَّا عَجُوزًا فِي الْغَابِرِينَ ١٣٥ ثُمَّ دَمَّرْنَا الْآخَرِينَ ١٣٦ وَإِنَّكُمْ لَتَمُرُّونَ عَلَيْهِم مُّصْبِحِينَ ١٣٧ وَبِاللَّيْلِ ۗ أَفَلَا تَعْقِلُونَ﴾\nAnd indeed, Lot was among the messengers. [So mention] when We saved him and his family, all, Except his wife among those who remained [with the evildoers]. Then We destroyed the others. And indeed, you pass by them in the morning . And at night. Then will you not use reason?\n(Quran, Surah-37, As-Saffat, Verses-133-138)\nThe wife of Lut(as) was not among the believers and was therefore left behind to perish. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَلَمَّا جَاءَتْ رُسُلُنَا إِبْرَاهِيمَ بِالْبُشْرَىٰ قَالُوا إِنَّا مُهْلِكُو أَهْلِ هَٰذِهِ الْقَرْيَةِ ۖ إِنَّ أَهْلَهَا كَانُوا ظَالِمِينَ ٣١ قَالَ إِنَّ فِيهَا لُوطًا ۚ قَالُوا نَحْنُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَن فِيهَا ۖ لَنُنَجِّيَنَّهُ وَأَهْلَهُ إِلَّا امْرَأَتَهُ كَانَتْ مِنَ الْغَابِرِينَ ٣٢﴾\nAnd when Our messengers came to Abraham with the good tidings, they said, \"Indeed, we will destroy the people of that Lot's city. Indeed, its people have been wrongdoers.\" [Abraham] said, \"Indeed, within it is Lot.\" They said, \"We are more knowing of who is within it. We will surely save him and his family, except his wife. She is to be of those who remain behind.\"\n(Quran, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verses-31,32)\nThat is, the wife of Lut(as) will not be saved from punishment but will be destroyed along with the other disbelievers due to her disbelief.\nIt is described in the Taurah that when Lut(as) reached the place Zoar at dawn, there was a rain of fire and sulphur on Sodom and Gomorrah and all living creatures including vegetation were destroyed. Lut(as)’s wife looked back and was turned into a pillar of salt. (Bible, Genesis, 19:23-26). Some scholars are of the opinion that the Dead Sea was formed due to this incident. That is why it is also called ‘Bahr Lut’. Its surface is about 400 mts. below sea level and hence gives the impression of a hole being formed due to the land being turned topsy-turvy and moreover the ruins of the tribe of Lut(as) are also found on its shores. ( See : Qasas- Anbiya: Najjar p.4:113)\nThis is the ultimate terrible end of the tribes who rebelled against Allah(swt). Instead of worshipping the one true God, they worshipped false gods and goddesses and the things created by Him(swt) and sought to fulfill their needs through them. Forsaking the true path prescribed by Allah(swt), they followed their own whims and fancies. They made fun of the messengers and prophets sent for their guidance by Allah(swt) and threatened to throw them out of their cities. They tormented the prophets in various ways. As a result they incurred the wrath of Allah(swt) and entire settlements were completely destroyed. This is a clear lesson for the wise.\nThe Holy Quran narrates the stories of numerous prophets so that the future generations take heed and learn lessons from them:\nلَقَدْ كَانَ فِي قَصَصِهِمْ عِبْرَةٌ لِّأُولِي الْأَلْبَابِ ۗ مَا كَانَ حَدِيثًا يُفْتَرَىٰ وَلَٰكِن تَصْدِيقَ الَّذِي بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَتَفْصِيلَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ وَهُدًى وَرَحْمَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يُؤْمِنُونَ\nThere was certainly in their stories a lesson for those of understanding. Never was the Qur'an a narration invented, but a confirmation of what was before it and a detailed explanation of all things and guidance and mercy for a people who believe.\n(Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-111)"],[196,"§Madina\nThe old name of Madina was Yathrib as mentioned in the Holy Quran:\nوَإِذْ قَالَت طَّائِفَةٌ مِّنْهُمْ يَا أَهْلَ يَثْرِبَ لَا مُقَامَ لَكُمْ فَارْجِعُوا\nAnd when a faction of them said, \"O people of Yathrib, there is no stability for you [here], so return [home].\"\n(Quran, Surah-33, Al-Ahzab, Verse-13)\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) changed the name of the city from Yathrib to Taiba because the meaning of Yathrib was ‘to rebuke or blame’ which was not liked by him. So he(saws) renamed it ‘Taiba’ which means ‘perfect’.\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said emphatically:\n“This is Taiba, this is Taiba, this is Taiba.”\n(Sahih Muslim 2942)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Allah(swt) has named Madina Taiba.”\n(Sahih Muslim 1385)\nBoth ‘Taaba’ and ‘Taiba’ have the same meaning – perfect or pure.\nThe city of Madina has many more names. Some say the number is about 94 which is not true as the information is based on some unreliable hadith.\nAs for Madina, the original name was ‘Madina-tur-Rasool’ which means the city of the prophet. By and by it got shortened to Madina and this name became the most popular one. The word ‘Madina’ is used four times in the Holy Quran. ( See: Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verses-101, 120; Surah-33, Al-Ahzab, Verse-60; Surah-63, Al-Munafiqun, Verse-8)."],[197,"§Madina’s inhabitants\nWhen there was a flood called Irum, the tribe of Saba in Yemen started running helter-skelter and the two Arabic tribes Ous and Khajraj migrated to Madina and settled there. A few Jews started out from Palestine in search of the Last Prophet(saws) who was described in the Taurah. When they reached the city of Taima, they thought that it was the place where the Holy Prophet(saws) would seek refuge and settled there. A few others went on further and settled in the city of Khyber and thought that the prophet will not come.\nA few historians are of the opinion that Madina was initially inhabited by the Jews and then the tribes of Ous and Khajraj settled there. But the facts are as mentioned above.\nThat is, the Jews occupied the entire region from Taima to Madina. They took over the entire trade. They owned the best of the date-farms and the Arabs became subservient to them. The Arabs came to know from these Jews that the Last Prophet(saws) would migrate to Madina and then with his help they would banish them from Arabia.\nBut when the Last Prophet(saws) did migrate to Madina, the Jews refused to accept his prophethood while they very well knew that this good news had been given by Musa(as). The reason was that the Holy Prophet(saws) was from the tribe of Bani-Ismael while the Jews were from the tribe of Bani-Israel. They considered themselves to be the best among the creation of Allah(swt) and so the Last Prophet(saws) could not be from any other tribe other than their tribe. Regarding this the Holy Quran says:\nالَّذِينَ آتَيْنَاهُمُ الْكِتَابَ يَعْرِفُونَهُ كَمَا يَعْرِفُونَ أَبْنَاءَهُمْ ۖ وَإِنَّ فَرِيقًا مِّنْهُمْ لَيَكْتُمُونَ الْحَقَّ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ\nThose to whom We gave the Scripture know him as they know their own sons. But indeed, a party of them conceal the truth while they know [it].\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-146; Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-20)\nThe two Arab tribes of Ous and Khajraj entered the fold of Islam and due to the exemplary help and service they rendered to the immigrants and the Holy Prophet(saws) earned the title ‘Ansar’.\nExcellence of Madina:\nThe excellence of Madina is narrated in a sahih hadith as:\n“Madina is like the furnace of the blacksmith which removes the impurities and retains the good things.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 7211 and Sahih Muslim, 1383)\nImportance of dying in Madina:\nIt is narrated in one sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Anybody who can die in Madina, let him endeavor to do so; because I shall intercede on his behalf.”\n(Tirmizi 3917 and Ahmad 2:74)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“Imaan will return to Madina just as a snake comes back to its hole.”\n(Sahih Bukhari 1876 and Sahih Muslim 147)\nSupplication for the prosperity of Madina:\n“O Allah(swt)! Make us love Madina just as we love Makka, and even more than that. O Allah(swt)! Increase our measures and keep us healthy and turn the diseases of Madina towards ‘Zuhfa’.\n(Sahih Bukhari 1888 and Sahih Muslim 1376)\nExcellence of settling in Madina:\nIt is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n“When Yemen triumphs, people will go there along with their families while Madina would be best for them if they only knew; when Syria triumphs, people will go there along with their families while Madina would be best for them if they only knew; when Iraq triumphs people will go there along with their families while Madina would be best for them if they only knew.”\n(Sahih Bukhari 1875 and Sahih Muslim 1388)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“When anybody leaves Madina hating it, Allah(swt) will cause better people to settle there. Madina is a furnace which removes the bad people from it. The Last Day will not occur till Madina removes all the unhappy people from it just as an iron furnace removes the impurities.”\n(Sahih Muslim 1381)\nIt is narrated in the sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Madina haram is from Aair mountain to the Saur mountain. Anybody who commits an atrocity there or gives refuge to a perpetrator of atrocity, the curse of Allah(swt), the angels and the people is on him. No recompense shall be accepted from him on the Day of Judgement to escape the punishment of Allah(swt).”\n(Sahih Bukhari 1870 and Sahih Muslim 1370)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“Anybody who even contemplates evil for the people of Madina, Allah(swt) shall dissolve him just as salt is dissolved in water.”\n(Sahih Muslim 1387)\nImportant places of Madina:\n1.Masjid-e-Nabawi: The reward of one salah offered in this mosque is equivalent to the reward of one hundred salahs.\n2.Raudah-e-Nabawi: After offering the Fard (obligatory) or Nafl (optional) salah in the Masjid-e-Nabawi, we should go to the grave of the Holy Prophet(saws) and offer our salutations as:\n“Assalamualaik ya Rasoolallah!”\nThen we should go to the graves of his companions Umar(ra) and Abu Bakr(ra) and offer our salutations.\n3.Riyazul Jannah: This is the area between the house of the Holy Prophet(saws) and his pulpit. (Sahih Bukhari 1196 and Sahih Muslim 1391)\n4.Pillars of Riyazul Jannah: The Holy Prophet(saws) liked to pray near these pillars. ( Sahih Bukhari 502 and Sahih Muslim 509)\n5.Masjid-e-Quba: This is the first mosque whose foundation was laid by the Holy Prophet(saws) when he migrated from Makka to Madina and was staying at Quba in the house of Bani Amr bin Ouf. The reward of offering one salah in this mosque is equivalent to the reward of performing one Umra. ( Nasai 2:37; Ibn-Majah 1412; Musnad Ahmad 3:487)\n6.Mount Uhud: When the Holy Prophet(saws) was returning from the war of Tabuk, the Holy Prophet(saws) saw Mount Uhud and said:\n“This is the mountain which loves me and I love it.”\n(Sahih Bukhari 4422 and Sahih Muslim 1392)\n7.Maqbara Baqi: We should go to the graveyard of Baqi and recite the following supplication:\n“Assalamualaikum daar Kaumim Muminin, antum saabiqoon, wa nahnu insha Allahubikum laahiqoon.”\n“You are the ones who shall go ahead and if Allah(swt) wills we will meet you.”\nThere are other important places in Madina like Masjid-e-Qiblatain, Masjid-e-Fatah, Shuhadaye-Uhud, Masjid-e-Jumua etc. It is not compulsory to visit them but they are important for understanding the life of the Holy Prophet(saws) from a historical view-point. So, without any expectation of reward, we can visit these places."],[198,"§Madyan\nKatura was one of the wives of Ibraheem(as) who had six children. One of the children was named Midyan and the offspring of Midyan settled in the region to the east Aqba and this entire region was called Madyan after him. These people were called Ashab-e-Aika or ‘the people of the garden.\nMadyan is described in the Holy Quran in two cases. In the first case it is mentioned that Shuaib(as) was sent as a prophet to Madyan (See : Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-85, Surah-11, Hud, Verse-84, Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot, Verse-36)\nIn the second case when Musa(as) killed a person and fearing for his life ran away from Egypt to Madyan( See : Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verse-40, Surah-28, Al-Qasas, Verse-22)\nWhen the Bani-Israel settled in Palestine there were frequent skirmishes with the people of Madyan. Once the people of Madyan captured the Bani-Israel and kept them prisoners for seven years. Then a judge named Jidan freed them.\nThe people of Madyan did trade along with farming. Their trade caravans went to various places like Egypt, Iraq,Yemen etc. The people of Madyan did not give correct measures due to which the prophet Shuaib(as) admonished them and asked them to stop doing so.(See : Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-85)\nBut the people of Madyan threatened Shuaib(as) that if he did not stop speaking out against their gods and goddesses and criticizing their deceit in the matter of measuring out less portions then they would banish him from Madyan. Thereupon they were seized by Allah(swt) in a terrible punishment due to which they were left face-down in their homes.( See : Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-91)"],[199,"§Magic\nMagic is a reality whose existence cannot be denied. Since ancient times magic has been described in various scriptures. Kings and emperors had magicians in their courts. That is why when Pharaoh(Firaun) asked the magicians to challenge Musa(as), they immediately questioned him, “If we win over Musa what prize will we get?” Pharaoh(Firaun) replied:\nقَالَ نَعَمْ وَإِنَّكُمْ إِذًا لَّمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِينَ\nHe said, \"Yes, and indeed, you will then be of those near [to me].\"\n(Quran, Surah-26, Ash-Shu’ara, Verse-42)\nIn Islam both learning and practicing magic are forbidden because magic can only be used to harm others. For example causing a rift between husband and wife. ( Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-102)\nThat is why we should seek refuge in Allah(swt) from the evil of magic. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ الْفَلَقِ ١ مِن شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ ٢ وَمِن شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ إِذَا وَقَبَ ٣ وَمِن شَرِّ النَّفَّاثَاتِ فِي الْعُقَدِ ٤ وَمِن شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ إِذَا حَسَدَ ٥﴾\nSay, \"I seek refuge in the Lord of daybreak .From the evil of that which He created .And from the evil of darkness when it settles .And from the evil of the blowers in knots .And from the evil of an envier when he envies.\"\n(Quran, Surah-113, Al-Falaq, Verses-1-5)\n‘Blowers on knots’ means the men and women who practice magic by tying knots and blowing on them. But the people who truly believe in Allah(swt) and seek refuge in Him(swt) should not fear such people. If they recite the surah Falaq and the following surah-Nas, before going to bed then magic and the satan can cause them no harm whatsoever. If magic has been done on somebody then that person should go to some righteous God-fearing scholar who can rid him of the bad effects with the help of verses from the Holy Quran."],[200,"§Majma’al Bahrain\nMajma’al Bahrain means the meeting point of two seas. This is described in the story of Musa(as) when he sets out to meet the slave of Allah(swt):\nوَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِفَتَاهُ لَا أَبْرَحُ حَتَّىٰ أَبْلُغَ مَجْمَعَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ أَوْ أَمْضِيَ حُقُبًا\nAnd [mention] when Moses said to his servant, \"I will not cease [traveling] until I reach the junction of the two seas or continue for a long period.\"\n(Quran, Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-60)\nWhere is this meeting point of the two seas? Among the many theories put forward, the best appears to be that this place is in the southern region of the Sinai desert where the inlet Aqba meets the inlet Suwais and then they flow into the Red Sea. This incident took place when the Bani-Israel had settled in the desert of Sina. One day while preaching, a question was posed to Musa(as), “Who is the most knowledgeable person?”. Musa(as) replied, “Myself.” Allah(swt) did not like this attitude and He(swt) told Musa(as),” A slave of mine who is more knowledgeable than you is in Majma’al Bahrain. Go to him. ( For more information refer to sahih Bukhari 4726, 4727) ( For detailed information see : Musa(as))"],[201,"§Majoos(Magians)\nThe Majoos have been described just once in the Holy Quran :\nإِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَالَّذِينَ هَادُوا وَالصَّابِئِينَ وَالنَّصَارَىٰ وَالْمَجُوسَ وَالَّذِينَ أَشْرَكُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَفْصِلُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ شَهِيدٌ\nIndeed, those who have believed and those who were Jews and the Sabeans and the Christians and the Magians and those who associated with Allah - Allah will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed Allah is, over all things, Witness.\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-17)\nMost of the scholars are of the opinion that Majoos means the fire-worshippers. They are also called ‘Parisees’. They belong to Iran. In the sixth century B.C., a person named ‘Zardusht’ who claimed prophethood was born and he propagated the theory of ‘two gods’. One is the god of good ‘Yazdan’ and the other is the god of evil ‘Arhaman’. Their religious scripture is ‘Dasateer’. When the light of Islam spread in Iran, it banished the darkness of the blind beliefs of the Magians. Now the Parisees are found in India and their population is steadily decreasing."],[202,"§Major sin\nSins as such are many but a few are major sins. Major sins are called ‘Kabair’ in Arabic which is the plural of ‘kabira’ that is, major sin.\nDefinition of major sins:\nAny sin for which the punishment is fixed, both in this world as well as in the next or any sin for which the Holy Prophet(saws) has cursed the sinner or has nullified his belief( imaan) are termed major sins.\nIn only one hadith seven types of major sins have been described. The Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Save yourselves from seven destructive deeds.” The people asked, “What are they O Apostle of Allah(saws)?”\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) replied:\nAttributing partners to Allah(swt).\nPracticing magic.\nKilling someone unjustly.\nConsuming interest.\nConsuming the wealth of orphans.\nRunning away from the battlefield.\nSlandering chaste women( Sahih Bukhari, 2766 and Sahih Muslim, 89)\nOne other major sin is to curse or abuse one’s parents.\nThe people asked, “O Apostle of Allah(swt), how can anybody curse his parents?”\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) replied,\n“This is because when a person abuses another person’s father, then the second person will also abuse the first person’s father. In the same way when a person abuses another person’s mother then the second person will abuse the first person’s mother.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 5973)\nOne other major sin is when the husband calls his wife to him and she refuses to come and the husband goes to bed angry. Such a wife is cursed by the angels till dawn.\n(See: Sahih Bukhari, 5193 and Sahih Muslim, 1436)\nOne other major sin is when a Muslim points a weapon at his brother, that is threatens him with it. The angels curse him whether the person is his own brother or not.\n(See : Sahih Muslim, 2616)\nWhen just the pointing of a weapon is such a great sin, then imagine the magnitude of the sin of killing one’s brother.\nThere are other sins which the Holy Prophet(saws) has warned against. The Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“O People Guard yourselves against two damning things.”\nThe people asked, “What are they?”\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) replied,\n“Relieving yourselves in the pathways used by people and in the shade of trees under which people take rest.”\n(See: Sahih Muslim, 269)\nThat is, the deeds which the Holy Prophet(saws) has cursed or damned are major sins. Hence it is imperative on the part of every Muslim to have a knowledge of these major sins and guard himself against them.\nThe list of major sins is quite long, but a few among them are as follows:\nGiving false testimony, gambling, stealing, robbery, committing atrocities against somebody, having anal intercourse with one’s wife, accepting bribes, hiding one’s knowledge, helping somebody and then making a show of it, harming one’s neighbor etc.\nWe should take care not to damn somebody who may be guilty of any of the major sins because it is possible that he may have repented for them or he may have done some good or pious deed which wipes out his sins.\nWe should also bear it in mind that all sins are not of equal degree. Some are such that the punishment is everlasting torment in hell. For example worshipping others besides Allah(swt). Such a person who attributes partners to Allah(swt) can never hope for forgiveness from Allah(swt).\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَغْفِرُ أَن يُشْرَكَ بِهِ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَن يَشَاءُ\nIndeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-48)\nإِنَّهُ مَن يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ فَقَدْ حَرَّمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ الْجَنَّةَ وَمَأْوَاهُ النَّارُ ۖ\nIndeed, he who associates others with Allah - Allah has forbidden him Paradise, and his refuge is the Fire.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-72)\nLuqman while instructing his son says:\nيَا بُنَيَّ لَا تُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ ۖ إِنَّ الشِّرْكَ لَظُلْمٌ عَظِيمٌ\n\"O my son, do not associate [anything] with Allah. Indeed, association [with him] is great injustice.\"\n(Quran, Surah-31, Luqman, Verse-13)\nIn Arabic, ‘Zulm’ means to remove a thing from its rightful place and keeping it elsewhere. So, what can be more unjust than worshipping someone instead of Allah(swt) Who has created us, given us sustenance, blessed us with good health and all sorts of comforts. The greatest injustice is attributing partners to Him(swt) in His sovereignty.\nIt is the opinion of Ibn-Abbas that the major sins are about seventy.\nOne other major sin is not to fulfill one’s religious obligations at the right time. For example salah, Zakat, Hajj, fasts of the Ramadan month etc. The one guilty of these is liable to be punished severely.\nThe people of hell will be asked:\n﴿مَا سَلَكَكُمْ فِي سَقَرَ ٤٢ قَالُوا لَمْ نَكُ مِنَ الْمُصَلِّينَ ٤٣ وَلَمْ نَكُ نُطْعِمُ الْمِسْكِينَ ٤٤ وَكُنَّا نَخُوضُ مَعَ الْخَائِضِينَ ٤٥ وَكُنَّا نُكَذِّبُ بِيَوْمِ الدِّينِ ٤٦ حَتَّىٰ أَتَانَا الْيَقِينُ ٤٧ فَمَا تَنفَعُهُمْ شَفَاعَةُ الشَّافِعِينَ ٤٨﴾\n[And asking them], \"What put you into Saqar?\" They will say, \"We were not of those who prayed, Nor did we used to feed the poor. And we used to enter into vain discourse with those who engaged [in it], And we used to deny the Day of Recompense .Until there came to us the certainty.\" So there will not benefit them the intercession of [any] intercessors.\n(Quran, Surah-74, Muddathir, Verses-42-48)\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith that the difference between a believer and a non-believer is namaz.\n(See: Sahih Muslim, 82)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“The difference between them and us is namaz and the one who forsakes namaz is guilty of ‘kufr’ or ‘disbelief’.”\n(See: Musnad Ahmad, 5:346 and Sunan)\nSimilarly it has been said about the people who do not give zakat:\nوَالَّذِينَ يَكْنِزُونَ الذَّهَبَ وَالْفِضَّةَ وَلَا يُنفِقُونَهَا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ فَبَشِّرْهُم بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ\nAnd those who hoard gold and silver and spend it not in the way of Allah - give them tidings of a painful punishment.\n(Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-34)\nThat is, major sins are of two kinds. The first kind are the ones which when committed entail a severe punishment. The second kind are the ones which when not performed will lead to a grievous punishment. Remaining sins are those which if we guard ourselves against the major sins, Allah(swt) will forgive them:\nالَّذِينَ يَجْتَنِبُونَ كَبَائِرَ الْإِثْمِ وَالْفَوَاحِشَ إِلَّا اللَّمَمَ ۚ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ وَاسِعُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ\nThose who avoid the major sins and immoralities, only [committing] slight ones. Indeed, your Lord is vast in forgiveness.\n(Quran, Surah-53, An-Najm, Verse-32)\nIt says at another place in the Holy Quran:\nإِن تَجْتَنِبُوا كَبَائِرَ مَا تُنْهَوْنَ عَنْهُ نُكَفِّرْ عَنكُمْ سَيِّئَاتِكُمْ وَنُدْخِلْكُم مُّدْخَلًا كَرِيمًا\nIf you avoid the major sins which you are forbidden, We will remove from you your lesser sins and admit you to a noble entrance [into Paradise].\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-31)\nIn this verse, Allah(swt) has given glad tidings of paradise to those who guard themselves against major sins because the good effects of good deeds wipe away the bad effects of bad deeds.\n(See : Quran, Surah-11, Hud, Verse-114)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“The five obligatory salahs wipe away the sins from one Jumu’a to another Jumu’a and those from one Ramadan to another, if one guards himself against the major sins.”\n(Sahih Muslim 233)\nIt is compulsory for every Muslim to have a knowledge of these major sins and try to guard himself against them lest he falls into the trap of major sins and loses his ultimate goal which is ‘Aakhirat’:\nخَسِرَ الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةَ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ هُوَ الْخُسْرَانُ الْمُبِينُ\nHe has lost [this] world and the Hereafter. That is what is the manifest loss.\n(Quran, Surah-22, Al-Hajj, Verse-11)\nAnd there is a lesson in this for the non-Muslims who consider Islam to be a religion of terrorism, if only they try to understand."],[203,"§Manat\nOf the three idols mentioned in Surah-53, An-Najm, Verse-20 of the Holy Quran, Manat is the name of the third idol. This has been erected in a place called Kudaid which is a city located on the shores of the Red Sea between Makka and Madina. The Arabs made offerings to it, sacrificed sheep and camels before it and circumambulated it just as they performed the ‘Tawaf’ of the Holy Kaaba. They supplicated to it for the fulfillment of their wishes. In other words they worshipped it and sought favours from it which should have been done from Allah(swt) alone. That is why after the victory over Makka, the Holy Prophet(saws) removed these idols from their worship-places. The trees which were being worshipped were cut down so that only Allah(swt) would be worshipped and favours sought from Him(swt) alone. On one occasion the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“The satan has lost all hope that anyone other than Allah(swt) will be worshipped here.”\nThis prophecy has proved true time and again because whenever the satan instigated the people to worship someone other than Allah(swt), there was some or the other slave of Allah(swt) who would make all the plots of the satan null and void.\nThis is the reason why even today, Saudi Arabia is a country where there are no tombs and graves which are worshipped or monasteries. Only mosques are present here where only Allah(swt) is worshipped. Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nوَأَنَّ الْمَسَاجِدَ لِلَّهِ فَلَا تَدْعُوا مَعَ اللَّهِ أَحَدًا\nAnd [He revealed] that the masjids are for Allah, so do not invoke with Allah anyone.\n(Quran, Surah-72, Al-Jinn, Verse-18)"],[204,"§Manna\nManna was a special type of food which was sent by Allah(swt) to the tribe of Bani-Israel when they were wandering in the desert of Sinai:\nوَظَلَّلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْغَمَامَ وَأَنزَلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوَىٰ ۖ كُلُوا مِن طَيِّبَاتِ مَا رَزَقْنَاكُمْ ۖ\nAnd We shaded you with clouds and sent down to you manna and quails, [saying], \"Eat from the good things with which We have provided you.\"\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-57)\n(Also see: Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-160 and Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verse-80)\nIn this way Manna was a type of food which would appear on the trees at dawn and turned into a sweetmeat. Even today a sweetmeat named Manna is quite popular in Syria."],[205,"§Maqaam-e-Mahmood\nAllah(swt) bestowed the Holy Prophet(saws) with numerous unique qualities and it is impossible to list out all of them. Scholars have written countless books about them. The book ‘Khasaais-Khubra’ ( great qualities) is one world-famous book. One of the favours is that Allah(swt) has granted the Holy Prophet(saws) the ‘Maqaam-e-Mahmood’ which means ‘praised position’.\nThe Holy Quran describes this as follows:\nوَمِنَ اللَّيْلِ فَتَهَجَّدْ بِهِ نَافِلَةً لَّكَ عَسَىٰ أَن يَبْعَثَكَ رَبُّكَ مَقَامًا مَّحْمُودًا\nAnd from [part of] the night, pray with it as additional [worship] for you; it is expected that your Lord will resurrect you to a praised station.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-79)\nWhat is this ‘Maqaam-e-Mahmood’? It has been narrated in the sahih hadith that it is an honoured position from which the Holy Prophet(saws) will intercede for his followers on the Day of Resurrection. (See: Intercession)\nWhat is going to happen is that on the Day of Resurrection, all creatures will be resurrected and they will be running hither-thither and there will be chaos and confusion everywhere. The people will run after their prophets but the prophets will say,”Today my Lord is very angry. So, I am worried about myself. Go to Muhammad(saws).” Then the people will go to the Last Prophet(saws). Muhammad(saws) will fall down in prostration.Allah(swt) will say:\n“Muhammad! Get up and ask what you want to ask.” The Holy Prophet(saws) will say, “Ummati- Ummati”. Allah(swt) will accept his intercession and say to the angels,”Go and whoever has even a grain of belief in his heart, admit him to paradise.”\nSo, this is ‘Maqaam-e-Mahmood’ which Allah(swt) has promised his slave Muhammad(saws). This is the high position from which he(saws) shall intercede for his followers.\n(See: Sahih Bukhari, 1474, 1475 and 1040)\nThe commentators of Quran have written extensively about this but the truth is only that which is corroborated by the sahih hadith because the correct explanation of the Holy Quran is given either by Quran itself or by the sahih hadith. The other commentaries come only after these. For detailed information see ‘Quran’."],[206,"§Marriage\nThe religion of Islam gives marriage a very important position. The Holy Prophet(saws) himself married and advocated marriage for the youth as is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n\"O young people! Whoever among you can marry, should marry, because it helps him lower his gaze and guard his modesty (i.e. his private parts from committing illegal sexual intercourse etc.), and whoever is not able to marry, should fast, as fasting diminishes his sexual power.\"\n(See: Sahih Bukhari-1905, and Sahih Muslim-1400)\nAll the prophets who were sent before the Last Prophet(saws) also married as is described in the Holy Quran:\nوَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلًا مِّن قَبْلِكَ وَجَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ أَزْوَاجًا وَذُرِّيَّةً\nAnd We have already sent messengers before you and assigned to them wives and descendants.\n(Quran, Surah-13, Ar-Ra’d, Verse-38)\nThis verse clearly negates the belief of some people who consider prophets to be some special beings like haloed creatures or reincarnations of God etc. and not ordinary humans. Based on this assumption many religious people remain celibate which clearly goes against the teachings of the prophets. In Islam the religious heads do not have any exceptions. What is allowed for others is allowed for them and what is forbidden for others is forbidden for them also and there is no distinction between them and others. The only difference is between those who have been given knowledge and those who haven’t:\nيَرْفَعِ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مِنكُمْ وَالَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْعِلْمَ دَرَجَاتٍ\nAllah will raise those who have believed among you and those who were given knowledge, by degrees.\n(Quran, Surah-58, Al-Mujadila, Verse-11)\nAs mentioned previously marriage was the way of the prophets.\nIt is narrated by the companion of the Holy Prophet(saws), Anas(ra) that a few companions had once assembled. One of them said,” I shall not marry.” One other said, “I shall not sleep at night but offer salah all night through.” Another said, “I shall fast and will not leave them.” When this was mentioned to the Holy Prophet(saws), he(saws) said,\n“What has happened to people that they do such things. Don’t they see that I sometimes fast and sometimes don’t, I sleep at night also and I pray during night also. I also marry and those that have left my path are not from among us.”\n(See: Sahih Bukhari-5063 and Sahih Muslim-1401)\nWhen one companion named Usman-bin-Mazoon decided to stop having intercourse with his wife, the Holy Prophet(saws) forbade him. If the Holy Prophet(saws) had allowed him to do it, then many would have castrated themselves.(See: Sahih Bukhari-5073 and Sahih Muslim-1402)\nOne main objective of marriage is procreation. Hence, while marrying, preference should be given to women who have more child-bearing capacity so that on the Day of Resurrection the Holy Prophet(saws) can feel superior to the other tribes(ummahs). ( See : Musnad Ahmad, 3:158)\nIslam allows a person to marry four women provided he can treat them all equally. If he feels that he cannot do justice to all his wives, then he should marry only one. (See: Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-3)\nMany do not understand the wisdom of allowing multiple wives in Islam and hence cast aspersions on it. If the human nature and the population of the women exceeding that of men is considered, then the logic behind this can be understood. If this is not allowed, then either people will commit adultery (not everybody but some of them) or the unmarried women instead of becoming somebody’s wife will become a burden on the society who will have nobody to safeguard them. To address these social problems, Islam has come up with this solution. On the other hand, the people who have multiple wives but do not treat them equally have also been severely criticized. Such people have been advised only one marriage instead of multiple marriages.\nBenefits of marriage:\n1.Guarding the chastity: The creation of man is based on chastity. That is why in order to satisfy the desires of human beings, the custom of marriage was initiated; else there would be no difference between men and animals.\n2.Affection between husband and wife:\nوَمِنْ آيَاتِهِ أَنْ خَلَقَ لَكُم مِّنْ أَنفُسِكُمْ أَزْوَاجًا لِّتَسْكُنُوا إِلَيْهَا وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَكُم مَّوَدَّةً وَرَحْمَةً ۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَآيَاتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ\nAnd of His signs is that He created for you from yourselves mates that you may find tranquillity in them; and He placed between you affection and mercy. Indeed in that are signs for a people who give thought.\n(Quran, Surah-30, Ar-Rum, Verse-21)\n3.Continuation of the human race: Marriage is the one means which ensures the existence of the human race on earth. Without marriage, man would cease to exist on earth.\n4.Guarding the character: That is, the character can be safeguarded only through marriage. If not immoral conduct would be prevalent everywhere.\nSome rules and commandments regarding marriage:\n1.Women with whom marriage is forbidden:\nحُرِّمَتْ عَلَيْكُمْ أُمَّهَاتُكُمْ وَبَنَاتُكُمْ وَأَخَوَاتُكُمْ وَعَمَّاتُكُمْ وَخَالَاتُكُمْ وَبَنَاتُ الْأَخِ وَبَنَاتُ الْأُخْتِ وَأُمَّهَاتُكُمُ اللَّاتِي أَرْضَعْنَكُمْ وَأَخَوَاتُكُم مِّنَ الرَّضَاعَةِ وَأُمَّهَاتُ نِسَائِكُمْ وَرَبَائِبُكُمُ اللَّاتِي فِي حُجُورِكُم مِّن نِّسَائِكُمُ اللَّاتِي دَخَلْتُم بِهِنَّ فَإِن لَّمْ تَكُونُوا دَخَلْتُم بِهِنَّ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَحَلَائِلُ أَبْنَائِكُمُ الَّذِينَ مِنْ أَصْلَابِكُمْ وَأَن تَجْمَعُوا بَيْنَ الْأُخْتَيْنِ إِلَّا مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ ۗ\nProhibited to you [for marriage] are your mothers, your daughters, your sisters, your father's sisters, your mother's sisters, your brother's daughters, your sister's daughters, your [milk] mothers who nursed you, your sisters through nursing, your wives' mothers, and your step-daughters under your guardianship [born] of your wives unto whom you have gone in. But if you have not gone in unto them, there is no sin upon you. And [also prohibited are] the wives of your sons who are from your [own] loins, and that you take [in marriage] two sisters simultaneously except for what is past.\n(See: Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-23)\nIt has been narrated in a sahih hadith that it is forbidden to have as wives at the same time both a woman and her father’s sister (paternal aunt) or a woman and her mother’s sister (maternal aunt).\n(See: Sahih Bukhari, 5109 and Sahih Muslim 1408)\n2.Shighar marriage: When a man agrees to marry the sister or daughter of another provided the other man marries the first man’s sister or daughter and there is an agreement that there will not be any dower paid, then such a marriage is termed ‘Shighar marriage’ and this has been forbidden by the Holy Prophet(saws) as it treats women like commodities which can be exchanged. (See : Sahih Bukhari, 5112 and Sahih Muslim 1415)\nBut if a dower has been decided then, it will not be termed ‘Shighar marriage’.\n3.One cannot marry disbelieving women until and unless they turn believers:\nوَلَا تَنكِحُوا الْمُشْرِكَاتِ حَتَّىٰ يُؤْمِنَّ ۚ وَلَأَمَةٌ مُّؤْمِنَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِّن مُّشْرِكَةٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ ۗ وَلَا تُنكِحُوا الْمُشْرِكِينَ حَتَّىٰ يُؤْمِنُوا ۚ وَلَعَبْدٌ مُّؤْمِنٌ خَيْرٌ مِّن مُّشْرِكٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَكُمْ ۗ أُولَٰئِكَ يَدْعُونَ إِلَى النَّارِ ۖ وَاللَّهُ يَدْعُو إِلَى الْجَنَّةِ وَالْمَغْفِرَةِ بِإِذْنِهِ ۖ وَيُبَيِّنُ آيَاتِهِ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ\nAnd do not marry polytheistic women until they believe. And a believing slave woman is better than a polytheist, even though she might please you. And do not marry polytheistic men [to your women] until they believe. And a believing slave is better than a polytheist, even though he might please you. Those invite [you] to the Fire, but Allah invites to Paradise and to forgiveness, by His permission. And He makes clear His verses to the people that perhaps they may remember.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-221)\nIt is allowed to marry the women of Ahle-Kitab (Jews and Christians).\n(See: Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-5)\nBut the condition is that the women are chaste and do not have lovers. The custom of having lovers was common since ancient times among the Ahle-Kitab. So, when Umar(ra) became the Caliph, he forbade the marrying of women from Ahle-Kitab. When he was asked if it was forbidden in Islam ( haram), he replied, “I do not say it is haram, but I fear that you may start marrying adulteresses.”\n(See : Ibn-Jareer Tabri 4:366)\nAdultery is one of the most hateful sins in Islam. That is why the believing men and women have been forbidden from marrying men and women who are not chaste. The Holy Quran says:\nالزَّانِي لَا يَنكِحُ إِلَّا زَانِيَةً أَوْ مُشْرِكَةً وَالزَّانِيَةُ لَا يَنكِحُهَا إِلَّا زَانٍ أَوْ مُشْرِكٌ ۚ وَحُرِّمَ ذَٰلِكَ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ\nThe fornicator does not marry except a [female] fornicator or polytheist, and none marries her except a fornicator or a polytheist, and that has been made unlawful to the believers.\n(Quran, Surah-24, An-Nur, Verse-3)\n4.If possible, it is better to have a look at the woman whom a person is going to marry as is narrated in a sahih hadith:\nIbn-Jabir narrates that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“If it is possible, have a look at the woman you are going to marry.”\nJabir(ra) narrates that he secretly tried to see the woman he was about to marry, till he finally saw her. ( See: Abu-Dawood 2082 and Mustdarak 2:165)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that it increases the affection between both of them. ( See : Tirmizi, 1087 and Ibn-Maaja 1885)\n5.If a man intends to marry a woman, then it is not allowed for another man to send a proposal to her. In case the first man divorces her, then it is allowed for another to marry her.( See : Sahih Bukhari, 5144 and Sahih Muslim 1412)\nAs soon as marriage takes place, the dower should be given as the Holy Quran says:\nوَآتُوا النِّسَاءَ صَدُقَاتِهِنَّ نِحْلَةً ۚ فَإِن طِبْنَ لَكُمْ عَن شَيْءٍ مِّنْهُ نَفْسًا فَكُلُوهُ هَنِيئًا مَّرِيئًا\n6.And give the women [upon marriage] their [bridal] gifts graciously. But if they give up willingly to you anything of it, then take it in satisfaction and ease.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-4)\nفَمَا اسْتَمْتَعْتُم بِهِ مِنْهُنَّ فَآتُوهُنَّ أُجُورَهُنَّ فَرِيضَةً ۚ وَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِيمَا تَرَاضَيْتُم بِهِ مِن بَعْدِ الْفَرِيضَةِ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كَانَ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمًا\nSo for whatever you enjoy [of marriage] from them, give them their due compensation as an obligation. And there is no blame upon you for what you mutually agree to beyond the obligation. Indeed, Allah is ever Knowing and Wise.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-24)\nA delay in giving the dower is allowed provided a definite time period is decided. That is, it is compulsory to pay the dower, either immediately or after some time. But, it has to be paid.\n7.The parents can freely give their daughter clothes, jewellery and house-hold items. The husband should neither take them nor demand anything from them. If he does so, then it is unlawful. The Holy Quran says:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَأْكُلُوا أَمْوَالَكُم بَيْنَكُم بِالْبَاطِلِ إِلَّا أَن تَكُونَ تِجَارَةً عَن تَرَاضٍ مِّنكُمْ ۚ\nO you who have believed, do not consume one another's wealth unjustly but only [in lawful] business by mutual consent.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-29)\nHence, if somebody has taken something from the wife's parents unknowingly, then he should return it as soon as possible so that the person who has consumed haram wealth is saved from hell-fire.\n8.Groom going in a procession to the bride’s place: This is a non-Islamic custom. It causes the bride’s parents and relatives unnecessary trouble. If the marriage is in another town, then it is allowed to take a few people along.\n9.Walima or the marriage banquet: This is ‘sunnah’ as is narrated in sahih hadith:\nWhen Abdur-Rehman-bin-Ouf married, the Holy Prophet(saws) said: “Have Walima even if it is with one goat.” ( Sahih Bukhari, 5168 and Sahih Muslim, 1428)\nWhen the Holy Prophet(saws) married Zainab(ra), he(saws) gave a walima of bread and meat. ( See : Sahih Bukhari, 5154 and Sahih Muslim, 1428).\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) gave the Walima after some of his marriages with just few handfuls of barley. ( See : Sahih Bukhari, 5172)\nThat is, it is sunnah to have Walima. A person can have walima according to his means and both the rich and the poor should be fed in it.\n10.Playing a tambourine in marriage: It is allowed to play the tambourine and sing in a decent way to express happiness during a wedding as is narrated in one sahih hadith:\n“The difference between what is lawful and what is unlawful is the playing of tambourine and singing at a wedding.”\nThat is, a marriage is declared openly either by the tambourine or by singing whereas adultery is committed secretly. This is the difference between marriage which is lawful and adultery which is unlawful.\n(See: Tirmizi-1088 Nasai, 6:1270, Ibn-Maaja, 1897)\nTambourine is a type of musical instrument used by fakirs etc. This can be used to express happiness during a wedding and also as a declaration of wedding. This is allowed whereas loud music and singing, dancing etc. are not allowed in Islam.\n11.The groom should give some gift to the bride as is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“The groom should give a gift to the bride on the wedding night. This increases the affection between them. And he should always remember that she is a weak creature who has been entrusted to him by Allah(swt) with just one word. So, he should be kind towards her. He should not hurt her in any way. The Holy Prophet(saws) always advocated good behavior towards women.”\n(See: Sahih Bukhari, 3331 and Sahih Muslim, 1468)\nOn one occasion the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“The true believer is the one who is the best in character and the best person is the one who is good towards his wife.”\n(See: Tirmizi, 1162)"],[207,"§Marwa\nMarwa is the name of a small hill located at a distance of about three hundred meters from the Holy Kaaba. It is described only once in the Holy Quran:\nإِنَّ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةَ مِن شَعَائِرِ اللَّهِ ۖ فَمَنْ حَجَّ الْبَيْتَ أَوِ اعْتَمَرَ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِ أَن يَطَّوَّفَ بِهِمَا\nIndeed, as-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. So whoever makes Hajj to the House or performs 'umrah - there is no blame upon him for walking between them.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-158)\n‘Sa’ee’ means ‘to try’. ‘Sa’ee’ during the Hajj and Umrah is the walking between the hills of Safa and Marwa. This commemorates an ancient incident. It is as follows. When Ibraheem(as) left his wife Hajira and infant son Ismael(as) in Makka, it was just a barren desert. It was uninhabited and there was nothing to eat or drink. The meager provisions which she had with her were exhausted after some time and she and her son started feeling thirsty. She climbed the nearby hill of Safa to see if she could find somebody or maybe something to eat or drink. When she could find nothing, she ran down and then climbed the other hill Marwa. In this way she made seven rounds between the hills of Safa and Marwa. The Holy Prophet(saws) explained,” It is to remember this that the sa’ee is performed.”\nSuddenly Hajira heard a voice and was perturbed. Then the voice was repeated. Gathering courage she went forward and saw that an angel was hitting the ground with his wings or feet. Soon a spring burst forth at that point which is called ‘zam-zam’. Hajira and her son had their fill of zam-zam and the angel gave them courage asking them not to worry. Later on after many years, Ismael(as) built the Holy Kaaba along with his father Ibraheem(as).(See: Sahih Bukhari, 3364)\nThe distance between Safa and Marwa is about two furlongs."],[208,"§Maryam\nMaryam who was the mother of Isa(as) is described in the Holy Quran and the study of her life can be divided into three parts:\nFirst part: The mother of Maryam made a promise that she would dedicate whatever is in her womb for the service of God.Then, when she gave birth to a girl she grew sad:\n﴿إِذْ قَالَتِ امْرَأَتُ عِمْرَانَ رَبِّ إِنِّي نَذَرْتُ لَكَ مَا فِي بَطْنِي مُحَرَّرًا فَتَقَبَّلْ مِنِّي ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ ٣٥ فَلَمَّا وَضَعَتْهَا قَالَتْ رَبِّ إِنِّي وَضَعْتُهَا أُنثَىٰ وَاللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا وَضَعَتْ وَلَيْسَ الذَّكَرُ كَالْأُنثَىٰ ۖ وَإِنِّي سَمَّيْتُهَا مَرْيَمَ وَإِنِّي أُعِيذُهَا بِكَ وَذُرِّيَّتَهَا مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيمِ ٣٦﴾\n[Mention, O Muhammad], when the wife of 'Imran said, \"My Lord, indeed I have pledged to You what is in my womb, consecrated [for Your service], so accept this from me. Indeed, You are the Hearing, the Knowing.\" But when she delivered her, she said, \"My Lord, I have delivered a female.\" And Allah was most knowing of what she delivered, \"And the male is not like the female. And I have named her Mary, and I seek refuge for her in You and [for] her descendants from Satan, the expelled [from the mercy of Allah].\"\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verses-35,36)\nWe come to know from the Holy Quran that Imran was the name of Maryam’s father, whereas the Bible mentions neither the name of Maryam’s father nor her mother. Matthew, Mark, Luke and John, start their respective Injeels from the birth of Isa(as).Muslim scholars in their commentaries have mentioned the name of Maryam’s mother as Hanna-bint-Faqudh. It is possible that they heard this from the Christian scholars. Two women named Hanna have been described in the Bible. One was Samuel’s mother and the other was someone called Hanna-bint-Fanoel. None of them was the mother of Maryam.\nIt is surprising that none of the Christian scholars have been able to give any information regarding the parents of Maryam. We only come to know from the Bible that she was from the family of Dawood(as).\nBecause Maryam was an orphan, her uncle Zakariya took up her responsibility:\nفَتَقَبَّلَهَا رَبُّهَا بِقَبُولٍ حَسَنٍ وَأَنبَتَهَا نَبَاتًا حَسَنًا وَكَفَّلَهَا زَكَرِيَّا\nSo her Lord accepted her with good acceptance and caused her to grow in a good manner and put her in the care of Zechariah.\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-37)\nIt was a miracle that Maryam was provided with food of various kinds and unseasonal fruits too:\nكُلَّمَا دَخَلَ عَلَيْهَا زَكَرِيَّا الْمِحْرَابَ وَجَدَ عِندَهَا رِزْقًا ۖ قَالَ يَا مَرْيَمُ أَنَّىٰ لَكِ هَٰذَا ۖ قَالَتْ هُوَ مِنْ عِندِ اللَّهِ ۖ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَرْزُقُ مَن يَشَاءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ\nEvery time Zechariah entered upon her in the prayer chamber, he found with her provision. He said, \"O Mary, from where is this [coming] to you?\" She said, \"It is from Allah. Indeed, Allah provides for whom He wills without account.\"\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-37)\nSecond part: In the second part she appears as a grown-up woman. In this stage she receives good news from Allah(swt):\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَتِ الْمَلَائِكَةُ يَا مَرْيَمُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ اصْطَفَاكِ وَطَهَّرَكِ وَاصْطَفَاكِ عَلَىٰ نِسَاءِ الْعَالَمِينَ ٤٢ يَا مَرْيَمُ اقْنُتِي لِرَبِّكِ وَاسْجُدِي وَارْكَعِي مَعَ الرَّاكِعِينَ ٤٣﴾\nAnd [mention] when the angels said, \"O Mary, indeed Allah has chosen you and purified you and chosen you above the women of the worlds. O Mary, be devoutly obedient to your Lord and prostrate and bow with those who bow [in prayer].\"\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verses-42,43)\nThat is she is being asked to obey the commands of her Lord. She has been given a very high status as she will be the mother of Isa(as). It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Among men, many have been successful in becoming model men, but the successful ones among the women have been three : Maryam-bint-Imran, Aasiya(wife of Pharaoh(Firaun)) and Aisha(ra). Their status among women is similar to that of the food Sareed among the other foods.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 3411 and Sahih Muslim, 2431)\nIn another sahih hadith only two successful women have been described. Maryam-bint-Imran and Khadija-bint-Khuwaylid.\n(Sahih Bukhari, 3815 and Sahih Muslim, 2130)\nWhen both the above hadith are taken in conjunction, the number of the women who are the best becomes four: Maryam, Aasiya, Aisha and Khadija(ra).\nThird part: It was due to the utterance of a single word ‘Kun’ by Allah(swt) that Maryam gave birth to Isa(as). For a detailed description study the life-history of Isa(as).\nBoth Maryam and her son Isa(as) were human beings. None of them had a share in divinity.\nمَّا الْمَسِيحُ ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ إِلَّا رَسُولٌ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِن قَبْلِهِ الرُّسُلُ وَأُمُّهُ صِدِّيقَةٌ ۖ كَانَا يَأْكُلَانِ الطَّعَامَ\nThe Messiah, son of Mary, was not but a messenger; [other] messengers have passed on before him. And his mother was a supporter of truth. They both used to eat food.\n(Quran, Surah-5, Ma’ida, Verse-75)\nWhat is meant here is that someone who needs food for sustenance cannot possibly be god.\nLuke, in his Injeel mentions a prayer of Maryam which proves that she was a human being:\nThen Mary said, “My heart is overflowing with praise of my Lord, my soul is full of joy in God my Saviour. For he has deigned to notice me, his humble servant and, after this, all the people who ever shall be will call me the happiest of women! The one who can do all things has done great things for me—oh, holy is his Name! Truly, his mercy rests on those who fear him in every generation. He has shown the strength of his arm, he has swept away the high and mighty. He has set kings down from their thrones and lifted up the humble. He has satisfied the hungry with good things, and sent the rich away with empty hands. Yes, he has helped Israel, his child: he has remembered the mercy that he promised to our forefathers, to Abraham and his sons for evermore!”\n(See: Luke, 1:46-55)\nAfter Isa(as) becomes a prophet, Maryam disappears; but Luke says that Isa(as) refuses to acknowledge his mother:\n“Isa was talking to the crowd.His mother and brother were standing outside.\nThey wanted to talk to Isa.Someone told Isa, “Look your mother and brother are standing outside.They want to talk to you.” Isa replied, “Who is my mother and who is my father ?”Isa(as) pointed to his disciples and said, “Look these are my mother and brother.”\n(See: Luke, 12:46-49)\nIt is very surprising that Isa(as) replied thus about his mother and refused to meet her. As against this, it says in the Holy Quran about Isa(as):\n﴿قَالَ إِنِّي عَبْدُ اللَّهِ آتَانِيَ الْكِتَابَ وَجَعَلَنِي نَبِيًّا ٣٠ وَجَعَلَنِي مُبَارَكًا أَيْنَ مَا كُنتُ وَأَوْصَانِي بِالصَّلَاةِ وَالزَّكَاةِ مَا دُمْتُ حَيًّا ٣١ وَبَرًّا بِوَالِدَتِي وَلَمْ يَجْعَلْنِي جَبَّارًا شَقِيًّا ٣٢﴾\n[Jesus] said, \"Indeed, I am the servant of Allah. He has given me the Scripture and made me a prophet. And He has made me blessed wherever I am and has enjoined upon me prayer and zakah as long as I remain alive .And [made me] dutiful to my mother, and He has not made me a wretched tyrant.\n(Quran, Surah-19, Maryam, Verses-30-32)\nWe come to know from the above verses that the Holy Quran gives Isa(as) a very high status and puts to rest the misconceptions that he could have treated his mother harshly.\nWe have no information as to what happened to Maryam after the ascent of Isa(as) to the heavens or when she passed away. Some scholars are of the opinion that after Isa(as), Maryam went away to one of his disciples and there she passed away in 48 A.D."],[209,"§Masjid-e-Aqsa\nMasjid-e-Aqsa means ‘the furthermost mosque’. This is described only once in the Holy Quran:\nسُبْحَانَ الَّذِي أَسْرَىٰ بِعَبْدِهِ لَيْلًا مِّنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ الْأَقْصَى\nExalted is He who took His Servant by night from al-Masjid al-Haram to al-Masjid al-Aqsa.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-1)\nHere Al-Masjid Al-Haram means ‘Baitullah’ which is in Makka and Masjid Al-Aqsa is the Baitul-Muqaddas in Palestine. This is also called ‘Khuds’ and ‘Shaleem’ and ‘Eeliya’ and is about 1300 kms from Makka.\nWe come to know from a sahih hadith that there is a time gap of about forty years between the construction of Masjid Al-Haram and Masjid Al-Aqsa. (See Sahih Bukhari, 3366 and Sahih Muslim, 520). As we all know Masjid Al-Haram was built by Ibraheem(as) and his son Ismael(as) ( See Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-127) and then forty years later Masjid Al-Aqsa was built maybe by Ibraheem(as) or by his offspring. Ibraheem(as) built the ‘Baitullah’ in Makka for his wife and son Ismael(as) for the worship of the One Lord Allah(swt) and so it follows that he must have built a mosque for his other son Ishaq(as) who remained in Palestine. Or it may be that his son Ishaq(as) built this mosque in Palestine. But it is not probable that the mosque built by him was the same one which was present till the time of the Holy Prophet(saws) because between the sixth century B.C and the first century B.C, the city of Baitul Muqaddas was destroyed again and again, worship-houses and churches were demolished etc. In fact in the fourth century the Roman emperor who had embraced Christianity completely devastated the Baitul-Muqaddas. Even after this the Christians continued to torment the Jews in various ways. They destroyed their worship-places. Only the Christians can answer as to why they behaved this way.\nThe Muslims never behaved this way. In fact Allah(swt) took the Holy Prophet(saws) from Masjid Al-Haram to Masjid Al-Aqsa which was built forty years after it in one night. That night the Holy Prophet(saws) even led the prayer for all the prophets( that is their spirits).\nThen when the disbelievers of Makka refused to believe in Isra( that is the journey of the Holy Prophet(saws) to Al-Aqsa), he(saws) described Al-Aqsa as if he(saws) was seeing it before him (See Sahih Bukhari 3886, and Sahih Muslim 17). In fact it is narrated in another sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said,”When I am describing Al-Aqsa, it has been brought in front of me. Seeing it, I am describing it” ( See Musnad Ahmad 2819). In 17 A.H. ( 637 A.D.) when the Muslims triumphed over Baitul-Muqaddas, the then Caliph Umar-bin-Khattab went to Baitul-Muqaddas, offered two rakat namaz in Al-Aqsa and ordered the mosque to be rebuilt because the Christians had made it a rubbish-dump. Then in 65 A.H. the Caliph Abdul-Malik and his son Waleed-bin Abdul-Malik rebuilt it. Today in the surrounding 35 acres are present Khubbatus-Saqra and Masjid-e-Umar along with Masjid-e-Aqsa and these are related to Islamic history. As for the Haikal built by Sulaiman(as), there is no information regarding it because the Christians repeatedly demolished Baitul-Muqaddas and razed the worship-houses of the Jews. And in fact when the second Caliph Umar-bin-Khattab was in Baitul-Muqaddas and was passing the Church of the holy sepulcher, the call for prayer was heard and the padre of the church opened the door and asked the Umar(ra) to pray there. But Umar(ra) did not do so saying that the Muslims may lay claim to the church saying that Umar(ra) had prayed there. And in the agreement made with the Christians, Umar(ra) laid down the condition that no worship-places will be razed.\nHence, the claim of the Jews that Masjid-Aqsa was built on Haikal of Sulaiman(as) has no basis or historical evidence.\nWe should also bear in mind that this was named ‘Al-Aqsa’ when it was not known where the next mosque would be built. It was only after the migration of the Holy Prophet(saws) to Madina that Masjid-e-Nabawi was built there. In this way, these are the three mosques to which we can travel in order to offer salah. The first is the Masjid-e-Haram in Makka, the second is the Masjid-e-Nabawi in Madina and the third is the Masjid-e-Aqsa in Baitul-Muqaddas and compared to Masjid-e-Nabawi this is the furthermost mosque."],[210,"§Masjid-e-Nabawi\nSee ‘Madina’."],[211,"§Masjidul-haram\nSee ‘Kaaba’."],[212,"§Masjid\nMasjid is a sacred place where the Muslims assemble in order to worship the One True Lord Allah(swt). The other religions also have their own worship-places but the difference is that in a Masjid only one Allah(swt) is worshipped. As the Holy Quran says:\nوَأَنَّ الْمَسَاجِدَ لِلَّهِ فَلَا تَدْعُوا مَعَ اللَّهِ أَحَدًا\nAnd [He revealed] that the masjids are for Allah, so do not invoke with Allah anyone.\n(Quran, Surah-72, Al-Jinn, Verse-18)\nIn the light of the above verse we can say that if in a masjid, anyone other than Allah(swt) is invoked or pictures etc. are kept then it becomes a place for idol-worship and ‘shirk’ which goes against the basic principle of monotheism of Islam. The previous tribes filled their worship-places with idols of prophets, angels, jinn and holy persons. That is why after the triumph over Makka, the Holy Prophet(saws) removed all the idols kept there. The idols of Ibraheem(as) were also among them. Attending the prayers in a mosque is a sign of true belief.\nإِنَّمَا يَعْمُرُ مَسَاجِدَ اللَّهِ مَنْ آمَنَ بِاللَّهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ\nThe mosques of Allah are only to be maintained by those who believe in Allah and the Last Day.\n(Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-18)\nBy ‘maintaining of mosques’ is meant ‘offering prayers in the mosques’ because it says in the preceding verse:\nمَا كَانَ لِلْمُشْرِكِينَ أَن يَعْمُرُوا مَسَاجِدَ اللَّهِ\nIt is not for the polytheists to maintain the mosques of Allah.\n(Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-17)\nWho can be a worse transgressor than the one who prevents others from praying in mosques:\nوَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّن مَّنَعَ مَسَاجِدَ اللَّهِ أَن يُذْكَرَ فِيهَا اسْمُهُ وَسَعَىٰ فِي خَرَابِهَا\nAnd who are more unjust than those who prevent the name of Allah from being mentioned in His mosques and strive toward their destruction.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-114)\nMasjid-e-Quba(The first mosque in the history of Islam):\nWhen the Holy Prophet(saws) migrated from Makka to Madina, he(saws) camped for a few days in a place called ‘Quba’ and there he(saws) laid the foundation of the first mosque. Offering two rakat namaz in this masjid is equivalent to one ‘Umra’."],[213,"§Masjid-e-Ziraar:\nThis is the masjid built by the hypocrites in order to cause a rift among the Muslims and was basically a plot to cause dissidence among the believers and they wanted the Holy Prophet(saws) to pray in it. Allah(swt) told the Holy Prophet(saws) about this evil plot and the following verses were revealed:\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ اتَّخَذُوا مَسْجِدًا ضِرَارًا وَكُفْرًا وَتَفْرِيقًا بَيْنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَإِرْصَادًا لِّمَنْ حَارَبَ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ مِن قَبْلُ ۚ وَلَيَحْلِفُنَّ إِنْ أَرَدْنَا إِلَّا الْحُسْنَىٰ ۖ وَاللَّهُ يَشْهَدُ إِنَّهُمْ لَكَاذِبُونَ ١٠٧ لَا تَقُمْ فِيهِ أَبَدًا ۚ لَّمَسْجِدٌ أُسِّسَ عَلَى التَّقْوَىٰ مِنْ أَوَّلِ يَوْمٍ أَحَقُّ أَن تَقُومَ فِيهِ ۚ فِيهِ رِجَالٌ يُحِبُّونَ أَن يَتَطَهَّرُوا ۚ وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُطَّهِّرِينَ ١٠٨ أَفَمَنْ أَسَّسَ بُنْيَانَهُ عَلَىٰ تَقْوَىٰ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرِضْوَانٍ خَيْرٌ أَم مَّنْ أَسَّسَ بُنْيَانَهُ عَلَىٰ شَفَا جُرُفٍ هَارٍ فَانْهَارَ بِهِ فِي نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ ۗ وَاللَّهُ لَا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الظَّالِمِينَ ١٠٩﴾\nAnd [there are] those [hypocrites] who took for themselves a mosque for causing harm and disbelief and division among the believers and as a station for whoever had warred against Allah and His Messenger before. And they will surely swear, \"We intended only the best.\" And Allah testifies that indeed they are liars. Do not stand [for prayer] within it - ever. A mosque founded on righteousness from the first day is more worthy for you to stand in. Within it are men who love to purify themselves; and Allah loves those who purify themselves. Then is one who laid the foundation of his building on righteousness [with fear] from Allah and [seeking] His approval better or one who laid the foundation of his building on the edge of a bank about to collapse, so it collapsed with him into the fire of Hell? And Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.\n(Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verses-107-109)\nAfter the revelation of the above verses, the Holy Prophet(saws) sent a few of his followers to fell the mosque.\nThe three chief Masjids:\n1.Al-Masjid-al-Haram : Makka\n2.Al-Masjid-e-Nabawi: Madina\n3.Al-Masjid-e-Aqsa : Palestine\nIn the first masjid, the reward of offering one salah is equivalent to the reward of offering one lakh salahs. In the second masjid, the reward of offering one salah is equivalent to the reward of offering one thousand salahs and in the case of the third masjid, it is equivalent to the reward of offering five hundred salahs. Hence, it has been commanded to journey to these mosques and offer salah. Other than these three mosques, it is forbidden to travel to other mosques as is narrated in a sahih hadith. ( See: Sahih Bukhari, 1863 and Sahih Muslim 827).\nMasjid-Juma:\nThis is the mosque where the Holy Prophet(saws) offered his first Friday prayer. When he(saws) was travelling from Quba to Madina and it was time for the Friday prayers, the Holy Prophet(saws) offered salah here and later on the people built a mosque here. There is no special reward for either travelling to this mosque or offering salah here and the reward for offering salah here is the same as offering it in any other ordinary mosque.\nMasjid-e-Qiblatain:\nThis is also a prominent masjid of Madina. This is called Masjid-e-Qiblatain, that is ‘masjid of two Qiblas’ because in this masjid, one salah was offered facing two Qiblas. The reason is as follows. In the beginning the Holy Prophet(saws) and others prayed facing the ‘Baitul-Muqaddas’ and when Makka was made the Qibla one person after offering salah came to Bani-Sulaim and saw them facing Baitul-Muqaddas. He shouted out aloud, “O People ! The Qibla has been changed.” The imam and the worshippers changed their direction of prayer from Baitul-Muqaddas to Kaaba in the state of salah itself. That is why this masjid is called ‘Masjid-e-Qiblatain’. The reward of offering salah in this mosque is the same as offering it in any other ordinary mosque."],[214,"§Menses\nThe monthly periods which the women have is called ‘Haiz’. The Holy Quran says in this regard:\n﴿وَيَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْمَحِيضِ ۖ قُلْ هُوَ أَذًى فَاعْتَزِلُوا النِّسَاءَ فِي الْمَحِيضِ ۖ وَلَا تَقْرَبُوهُنَّ حَتَّىٰ يَطْهُرْنَ ۖ فَإِذَا تَطَهَّرْنَ فَأْتُوهُنَّ مِنْ حَيْثُ أَمَرَكُمُ اللَّهُ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ التَّوَّابِينَ وَيُحِبُّ الْمُتَطَهِّرِينَ ٢٢٢ نِسَاؤُكُمْ حَرْثٌ لَّكُمْ فَأْتُوا حَرْثَكُمْ أَنَّىٰ شِئْتُمْ ۖ وَقَدِّمُوا لِأَنفُسِكُمْ ۚ ٢٢٣﴾\nAnd they ask you about menstruation. Say, \"It is harm, so keep away from wives during menstruation. And do not approach them until they are pure. And when they have purified themselves, then come to them from where Allah has ordained for you. Indeed, Allah loves those who are constantly repentant and loves those who purify themselves.\" Your wives are a place of sowing of seed for you, so come to your place of cultivation however you wish and put forth [righteousness] for yourselves.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-222,223)\nThat is, it is forbidden to have intercourse with a menstruating woman till she purifies herself after the completion of her cycle and intercourse should be vaginal and not anal as conception takes place only through the former method. We now present a few commandments regarding menstruating women:\n1.Such women are forbidden from praying.\n2.Such women are forbidden from fasting in the month of Ramadan; but when they purify themselves then they should fast for the missed number of days and these are called ‘Qaza’ fasts and are obligatory.\n3.Such women are forbidden from circumambulating the Holy Kaaba. If a woman has her periods when she goes on hajj then she should wait till she is pure and then perform the ‘Tawaaf’ and the other rites.\n4.Such women can go to ‘Arafat’ but cannot perform the ‘Tawaf-e-Ifaaza’ which is one of the pillars of Hajj. She should wait till she is pure and then perform it. In case her companions are returning and she cannot stay in Makka alone, then she can perform the ‘Tawaf-e-Ifaaza’ as otherwise her Hajj will remain incomplete.\n5.Such women can neither touch nor read the Holy Quran. But if the woman is a teacher or student then she can wear gloves and read the Holy Quran and turn the pages using a pen etc. because this is a necessity. In other cases she is forbidden from touching or reading the Holy Quran.\n6.A woman cannot be divorced when she is having her periods. If she is divorced in such a state, is the divorce valid or not? The scholars have differing opinions on this point.\n7.As soon as menses is over, she should have a complete bath as soon as possible. If water is unavailable or if the use of water is harmful in some way, then tayammum can be performed. As soon as the difficulty is over, a proper bath should be taken.\n8.Only intercourse with a menstruating woman is forbidden. Staying with her, sleeping with her, eating and drinking with her, fondling her etc. are permissible.\nIt is narrated in a few hadith that in case a man has intercourse with a menstruating woman, then he has to give one dinar in charity as compensation. But the scholars are of the opinion that these hadith are not reliable."],[215,"§Meraj\nSee ‘Isra’."],[216,"§Michael\nMichael is the name of an angel who has been described in the Holy Quran at only one place:\nمَن كَانَ عَدُوًّا لِّلَّهِ وَمَلَائِكَتِهِ وَرُسُلِهِ وَجِبْرِيلَ وَمِيكَالَ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ عَدُوٌّ لِّلْكَافِرِينَ\nWhoever is an enemy to Allah and His angels and His messengers and Gabriel and Michael - then indeed, Allah is an enemy to the disbelievers.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-98)\nThe Jews considered Michael to be their friend but perceived Jibrael as their enemy. Condemning such attitude, Allah(swt) says that all angels are His(swt) slaves whom He(swt) has created and allocated various tasks to and hence enmity with any of them is tantamount to enmity with Allah(swt).\nIn the Hebrew language Michael is called Miquael which means ‘Who is like God?’ In the Bible, Michael has been mentioned as the chief messenger of heaven. ( Daniel 10:13, 12:1)\nAnd this is the same Michael who will wake up the dead on the Day of Resurrection. ( See Thessalonians 4:16)\nBut according to some Islamic scriptures, Israfeel will blow the trumpet on the Day of Resurrection and the dead shall rise from their graves. But the chain of narrators of none of these hadith is reliable. The popular opinion is that the angel who will blow the trumpet will be Israfeel. Israfeel has been described in the sahih hadith but not in the context of the trumpet-blower but in other contexts. ( For example Sahih Muslim 770)"],[217,"§Middle-path\n‘Middle’ is the meaning of the Arabic word ‘vast’ which also means ‘top’ or ‘perfect’. That is why it has been said that you are from the ‘middle’ or ‘top’ tribe.\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَاكُمْ أُمَّةً وَسَطًا لِّتَكُونُوا شُهَدَاءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَيَكُونَ الرَّسُولُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيدًا ۗ\nAnd thus we have made you a just community that you will be witnesses over the people and the Messenger will be a witness over you.\n(Quran, Surah-2, al-Baqara, Verse-143)\nOne of the many unique qualities of the religion of Islam is that it is a ‘middle’ religion:\nBefore Islam the people of the book, especially the Christians introduced many new innovations, started practicing them and then caused deviations in the religion. With reference to this the Holy Quran says:\nقُلْ يَا أَهْلَ الْكِتَابِ لَا تَغْلُوا فِي دِينِكُمْ غَيْرَ الْحَقِّ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُوا أَهْوَاءَ قَوْمٍ قَدْ ضَلُّوا مِن قَبْلُ وَأَضَلُّوا كَثِيرًا وَضَلُّوا عَن سَوَاءِ السَّبِيلِ\nSay, \"O People of the Scripture, do not exceed limits in your religion beyond the truth and do not follow the inclinations of a people who had gone astray before and misled many and have strayed from the soundness of the way.\"\n(Quran, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-77)\nيَا أَهْلَ الْكِتَابِ لَا تَغْلُوا فِي دِينِكُمْ وَلَا تَقُولُوا عَلَى اللَّهِ إِلَّا الْحَقَّ ۚ إِنَّمَا الْمَسِيحُ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ وَكَلِمَتُهُ أَلْقَاهَا إِلَىٰ مَرْيَمَ وَرُوحٌ مِّنْهُ ۖ فَآمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِ ۖ وَلَا تَقُولُوا ثَلَاثَةٌ ۚ انتَهُوا خَيْرًا لَّكُمْ ۚ إِنَّمَا اللَّهُ إِلَٰهٌ وَاحِدٌ ۖ سُبْحَانَهُ أَن يَكُونَ لَهُ وَلَدٌ ۘ لَّهُ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ ۗ وَكَفَىٰ بِاللَّهِ وَكِيلًا\nO People of the Scripture, do not commit excess in your religion or say about Allah except the truth. The Messiah, Jesus, the son of Mary, was but a messenger of Allah and His word which He directed to Mary and a soul [created at a command] from Him. So believe in Allah and His messengers. And do not say, \"Three\"; desist - it is better for you. Indeed, Allah is but one God. Exalted is He above having a son. To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. And sufficient is Allah as Disposer of affairs.\n(Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-171)\nBy ‘His Word’ is meant the Arabic word ‘Kun’ using which Allah(swt) has created this entire Creation. The meaning of ‘Kun’ is ‘Be’. Allah(swt) is All-Powerful and if He(swt) wants something to happen He(swt) just has to say the word ‘Kun’ and the task is accomplished. By ‘soul’ or ‘spirit’ is meant what Jibrail blew towards Maryam upon the command of Allah(swt).This is the thing which has misled the Christians into believing Jesus(as) to be the son of God while in fact what has been mentioned in the Injeels regarding the relationship between a father and a son is to explain the relationship between a Creator and His slave. The Christians misunderstand it to literally mean a father and son. Since ancient times there have been many misinterpretations and deviations regarding Allah(swt). Some say that He(swt) is without any qualities; He can neither hear nor see, He can neither speak nor walk, He is neither above nor below, He is neither in front nor behind, neither left nor right. They say that He(swt) is just an imaginary power and nothing else. Some have divided Him into three parts and say that He is one in three and three in one. Some have made Him into various gods and goddesses depending on His attributes and the number has gone up from 33 to 33 crores. And they say that the entire Creation and all the gods and goddesses are His ash. In this way the pure concept of monotheism was corrupted. As the Holy Quran is the Last book of Allah(swt), it condemns this polytheism categorically at numerous places and reiterates the beautiful truth of monotheism.\nIf we just study surah-112, Al-Ikhlaas consisting of a total of four verses, we can understand the Greatness and Oneness of Allah(swt):\n﴿قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ ١ اللَّهُ الصَّمَدُ ٢ لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يُولَدْ ٣ وَلَمْ يَكُن لَّهُ كُفُوًا أَحَدٌ ٤﴾\nSay, \"He is Allah, [who is] One, Allah, the Eternal Refuge. He neither begets nor is born, Nor is there to Him any equivalent.\"\n(Quran, Surah-112, Al-Ikhlaas, Verses-1-4)\nAs mentioned earlier, the Holy Quran lays down the rules for leading a successful life. That is why we need to adopt a middle-path regarding the Quranic teachings.\nWe get a glimpse of this middle-path from the life of Muhammad(saws). It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“When there were two solutions to a problem and the Holy Prophet(saws) was given the freedom to choose one, then he would choose the easier one if there was no sin involved and if the path was sinful then he would be among the ones to stay as far away from it as possible. The Holy Prophet(saws) never took revenge against anybody who had harmed him. But if somebody transgressed the limits set by Allah(swt), then he(saws) punished them for the sake of Allah(swt).”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 3560 and Sahih Muslim, 2327)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Allah(swt) has sent me as a teacher and one who makes things easy.”\n(Sahih Muslim, 1478)\nWhen the Holy Prophet(saws) sent somebody as a governor or administrator, he(saws) instructed him to make things easy. For example when he(saws) sent Abu-Musa and Mu’aaz to Yemen, he(saws) said:\n“Make things easy not difficult, give cheers and glad tidings and do not create hatred.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 4341 and Sahih Muslim, 1733)\nTaking the middle-path in matters of worship:\nAllah(swt) has created man for His(swt) worship. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَمَا خَلَقْتُ الْجِنَّ وَالْإِنسَ إِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُونِ ٥٦﴾\nAnd I did not create the jinn and mankind except to worship Me.\n(Quran, Surah-51, Adh-Dhariyat, Verse-56)\nThat is, not for the worship of someone else. We need to bear it in mind that the wish of Allah(swt) that we should worship Him(swt) alone is but natural. And moreover this is not by force or compulsion as in that case man would have no choice but to worship Allah(swt) as in the case of the angels:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا قُوا أَنفُسَكُمْ وَأَهْلِيكُمْ نَارًا وَقُودُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجَارَةُ عَلَيْهَا مَلَائِكَةٌ غِلَاظٌ شِدَادٌ لَّا يَعْصُونَ اللَّهَ مَا أَمَرَهُمْ وَيَفْعَلُونَ مَا يُؤْمَرُونَ\nO you who have believed, protect yourselves and your families from a Fire whose fuel is people and stones, over which are [appointed] angels, harsh and severe; they do not disobey Allah in what He commands them but do what they are commanded.\n(Quran, Surah-66, At-Tahrim, Verse-6)\nIf it had been the command of Allah(swt), it would get fulfilled:\nبَدِيعُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۖ وَإِذَا قَضَىٰ أَمْرًا فَإِنَّمَا يَقُولُ لَهُ كُن فَيَكُونُ\nOriginator of the heavens and the earth. When He decrees a matter, He only says to it, \"Be,\" and it is.\n(Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-117)\nBut, Allah(swt) has given man the freedom of choice and based on his choice he shall be judged on the Day of Judgement.\nAs man also has to take care of his worldly affairs, Allah(swt) wishes that man worship Him(swt) according to his wish and that he should not go to extremes in the matter of religion and worship:\nوَرَهْبَانِيَّةً ابْتَدَعُوهَا مَا كَتَبْنَاهَا عَلَيْهِمْ إِلَّا ابْتِغَاءَ رِضْوَانِ اللَّهِ فَمَا رَعَوْهَا حَقَّ رِعَايَتِهَا ۖ\nmonasticism, which they innovated; We did not prescribe it for them except [that they did so] seeking the approval of Allah. But they did not observe it with due observance.\n(Quran, Surah-57, Al-Hadid, Verse-27)\nSo, just as Islam prescribes middle-path in all matters, even in the matter of worship of Allah(swt), it advocates the middle-path.\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Three people came to the house of the Holy Prophet(saws).They wished to know how the Holy Prophet(saws) worshipped Allah(swt). They understood very little of what was said to them in this regard and said, ”How can we reach the stature of the Holy Prophet(swt). Allah(swt) has forgiven all his(saws) past and future sins.” Then one of them said, “I shall always pray the whole night.” The second person said, “I shall fast on all days.” The third person said, “I shall stay away from women and shall never marry.”\nWhen the Holy Prophet(saws) came home, he was informed of what these three people had said. The Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“Have you said this? I swear in the name of Allah(swt) that I am the one who fears Allah(swt) the most, but I sometimes fast and sometimes do not. I pray during the night and also sleep and I also marry. So, whoever strays from my path is not from among us.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 5063 and Sahih Muslim, 1401)\nTreading the middle-path in leading one’s life:\n1.Middle-path in matters of eating and drinking:\nThe Holy Quran says:\nيَا بَنِي آدَمَ خُذُوا زِينَتَكُمْ عِندَ كُلِّ مَسْجِدٍ وَكُلُوا وَاشْرَبُوا وَلَا تُسْرِفُوا ۚ إِنَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُسْرِفِينَ\nO children of Adam, take your adornment at every masjid, and eat and drink, but be not excessive. Indeed, He likes not those who commit excess.\n(Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-31)\nكُلُوا مِن ثَمَرِهِ إِذَا أَثْمَرَ وَآتُوا حَقَّهُ يَوْمَ حَصَادِهِ ۖ وَلَا تُسْرِفُوا ۚ إِنَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُسْرِفِينَ\nEat of [each of] its fruit when it yields and give its due [zakah] on the day of its harvest. And be not excessive. Indeed, He does not like those who commit excess.\n(Quran, Surah-6, Al-An’am, Verse-141)\n2.Middle-path in matters of pious deeds and charity:\nوَالَّذِينَ إِذَا أَنفَقُوا لَمْ يُسْرِفُوا وَلَمْ يَقْتُرُوا وَكَانَ بَيْنَ ذَٰلِكَ قَوَامًا And [they are] those who, when they spend, do so not excessively or sparingly but are ever, between that, [justly] moderate.\n(Quran, Surah-25, Al-Furqan, Verse-67)\nFollowing the command of Allah(swt), it is best to spend in the path of Allah(swt). But if we go to extremes in this matter, it can lead to many complications. At another place in the Holy Quran it says in this regard:\nوَلَا تَجْعَلْ يَدَكَ مَغْلُولَةً إِلَىٰ عُنُقِكَ وَلَا تَبْسُطْهَا كُلَّ الْبَسْطِ فَتَقْعُدَ مَلُومًا مَّحْسُورًا\nAnd do not make your hand [as] chained to your neck or extend it completely and [thereby] become blamed and insolvent.\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-29)\n3.Middle-path with regard to revenge:\nوَجَزَاءُ سَيِّئَةٍ سَيِّئَةٌ مِّثْلُهَا ۖ فَمَنْ عَفَا وَأَصْلَحَ فَأَجْرُهُ عَلَى اللَّهِ ۚ إِنَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الظَّالِمِينَ\nAnd the retribution for an evil act is an evil one like it, but whoever pardons and makes reconciliation - his reward is [due] from Allah. Indeed, He does not like wrongdoers.\n(Quran, Surah-42, Ash-Shura, Verse-40)\nThat is, if somebody has been wronged against, then it is allowed for him to seek retribution; but he should not go to extremes in this regard but try to be moderate. The revenge should be proportionate to the injustice done against him. If the victim decides to forgive and forget, then it is best for him because he shall get his reward from Allah(swt).\nوَإِنْ عَاقَبْتُمْ فَعَاقِبُوا بِمِثْلِ مَا عُوقِبْتُم بِهِ ۖ وَلَئِن صَبَرْتُمْ لَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لِّلصَّابِرِينَ\nAnd if you punish [an enemy, O believers], punish with an equivalent of that with which you were harmed. But if you are patient - it is better for those who are patient.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-126)\nThat is, we are allowed to seek revenge but only to the extent of the amount of harm done to us. If we cross the limits then we shall be among the transgressors.\nThis concerns mainly the ancient tribes who would kill ten people to avenge the killing of one of their tribe. It says at one other place:\nوَمَن قُتِلَ مَظْلُومًا فَقَدْ جَعَلْنَا لِوَلِيِّهِ سُلْطَانًا فَلَا يُسْرِف فِّي الْقَتْلِ ۖ إِنَّهُ كَانَ مَنصُورًا\nAnd whoever is killed unjustly - We have given his heir authority, but let him not exceed limits in [the matter of] taking life. Indeed, he has been supported [by the law].\n(Quran, Surah-17, Bani-Israel, Verse-33)\nThat is, as revenge for the killing of one person do not kill two-three or more people and do not unnecessarily torment them. The best thing would be to forgive the culprits or come to an understanding and this is the middle-path.\n4.Middle-path while dealing with the non-Muslims:\nIslam is a religion which advocates peace. That is why Prophet Muhammad(saws) has been sent as ‘Rahmatul-lil-alameen’ which means ‘mercy for the entire world’. After the triumph over Makka, the Holy Prophet(saws) even forgave those enemies who had plotted his murder and due to whom he(saws) had to migrate to Madina. He(saws) forgave his enemies on many occasions and we can see the greatness of his life-history from these incidents.\nThe Holy Quran says that we should treat the non-Muslims well:\nلَّا يَنْهَاكُمُ اللَّهُ عَنِ الَّذِينَ لَمْ يُقَاتِلُوكُمْ فِي الدِّينِ وَلَمْ يُخْرِجُوكُم مِّن دِيَارِكُمْ أَن تَبَرُّوهُمْ وَتُقْسِطُوا إِلَيْهِمْ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُقْسِطِينَ\nAllah does not forbid you from those who do not fight you because of religion and do not expel you from your homes - from being righteous toward them and acting justly toward them. Indeed, Allah loves those who act justly.\n(Quran, Surah-60, Al-Mumtahina, Verse-8)\nIf someone has embraced Islam but his parents are disbelievers, then he should treat them with kindness:\nوَإِن جَاهَدَاكَ عَلَىٰ أَن تُشْرِكَ بِي مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهِ عِلْمٌ فَلَا تُطِعْهُمَا ۖ وَصَاحِبْهُمَا فِي الدُّنْيَا مَعْرُوفًا\nBut if they endeavor to make you associate with Me that of which you have no knowledge, do not obey them but accompany them in [this] world with appropriate kindness.\n(Quran, Surah-31, Luqman, Verse-15)\nNeither are all the Muslims enemies of the non-Muslims nor are all non-Muslims the enemies of Muslims. In fact, Islam was first conveyed to the non-Muslims and we have a huge responsibility upon us to convey the message of Islam to the non-Muslims.\nAs for the jihad against the non-Muslims, this is in fact a fight to remove crime, aggression and injustice from human society and not for spreading chaos:\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ يَأْمُرُ بِالْعَدْلِ وَالْإِحْسَانِ وَإِيتَاءِ ذِي الْقُرْبَىٰ وَيَنْهَىٰ عَنِ الْفَحْشَاءِ وَالْمُنكَرِ وَالْبَغْيِ ۚ يَعِظُكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُونَ\nIndeed, Allah orders justice and good conduct and giving to relatives and forbids immorality and bad conduct and oppression. He admonishes you that perhaps you will be reminded.\n(Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-90)\nIf we compare jihad with nuclear wars which in a few seconds kill lakhs of men and women and children and old people, we understand that Islam does not permit these atrocities. The Holy Prophet(saws) in just a few years established peace in the Arab countries from Yemen to Iraq. So, the uninformed who say that jihad creates chaos should first study the Holy Quran. The things which these people do in the name of spreading peace are only causing unrest everywhere. Peace can only be established if we implement the Islamic principles with regard to human conduct and social interaction with purity of purpose.\nIn this way, Islam advocates the middle-path in all matters so that a peaceful society is established in which both the Muslims and the non-Muslims co-exist without any feeling of fear or hatred.\nHence we conclude that it is imperative for every Muslim to follow the middle-path and be moderate in all matters so that his life becomes a lesson to others."],[218,"§Misr\n‘Misr’ which is also called Egypt is derived from the Hebrew word ‘Misraim’ who was the son of ‘Haam’, the son of Nuh(as). Egyptian history dates back to 5000 B.C. The stone inscriptions of those ages are similar to the inscriptions of Mohenjodaro and we understand that both these tribes used animal images to form a language and the Egyptians called these ‘hieroglyphics’. In those ancient times, superstitions and blind beliefs were prevalent and as a result the Egyptians had made the sun, the moon, the stars their gods and goddesses. Sun was called ‘Ra’ and the earth was called ‘Jab’ and were worshipped. They believed that the dead also needed food, drink, clothes, servants, utensils etc. just like the living and therefore instead of burying their dead, they put the corpse in a room along with food, drink, clothes etc so the dead could use them according to their need. They also believed that the soul would return to the dead body and for this reason they embalmed their dead with various potions and liniments. Some of the bodies found in the pyramids are more than five thousand years old, but as they have been embalmed they have not decomposed and are in a preserved state. But all these are things of the past. Today most of them are Muslims and no longer superstitious. Many incidents concerning many prophets are connected with Egypt and hence it has been described again and again in both the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith. When Ibraheem(as) migrated to Egypt he came to know that its ruler was a tyrant. He abducted good-looking women. So, he took away Sara, the beautiful wife of Ibraheem(as). But due to the mercy of Allah(swt), the wicked king could not even come near Sara. So much so that in the end he sent away Sara along with his slave Hajira as a gift. This is the same Hajira whom Ibraheem(as) married and who gave birth to Ismael(as). Prophet Muhammad(saws) was from the tribe of this same Ismael(as). (See Sahih Bukhari, 2217 and Sahih Muslim, 2371)\n‘Misr’ is also described in the story of Yusuf(as). He was sold in Egypt and the person who bought him was the king of Egypt. ( See : Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-21)\nThen, the parents of Yusuf(as) come to Egypt and Yusuf(as) seats them on a high pedestal.( See : Quran, Surah-12, Yusuf, Verse-99)\nAfter this, the descendants of Yaqub(as) namely Bani-Israel stayed in Misr for about 300 years and then left it to go to the desert Sinai (which is a part of Egypt) along with Musa(as) and spent 40 years there. The Holy Prophet(saws) wrote many letters to various kings in 9 A.H. One of them was to the king of Egypt, Muqauqis which ran as follows:\n\"In the name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Muqauqis, the Chief of the Copts.\nPeace be upon him who follows the guidance.\n\"After this, I call you to Islam that you may find peace, and God will give you a double reward. If you reject, then on you shall be the sin of your countrymen. O people of the Book, come to that which is common between you and us; that we will serve none but Allah, nor associate aught with him, nor take others for lords besides God. But if you turn away, then say: bear witness that we are Muslims.\"\nThen he(saws) wrote the following verse of the Holy Quran:\nقُلْ يَا أَهْلَ الْكِتَابِ تَعَالَوْا إِلَىٰ كَلِمَةٍ سَوَاءٍ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمْ أَلَّا نَعْبُدَ إِلَّا اللَّهَ وَلَا نُشْرِكَ بِهِ شَيْئًا وَلَا يَتَّخِذَ بَعْضُنَا بَعْضًا أَرْبَابًا مِّن دُونِ اللَّهِ ۚ فَإِن تَوَلَّوْا فَقُولُوا اشْهَدُوا بِأَنَّا مُسْلِمُونَ\nSay, \"O People of the Scripture, come to a word that is equitable between us and you - that we will not worship except Allah and not associate anything with Him and not take one another as lords instead of Allah.\" But if they turn away, then say, \"Bear witness that we are Muslims [submitting to Him].\"\n(Quran, Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-64)"],[219,"§Monasticism(Rahbaniyat)\nPenance and asceticism means to give up the comforts of this worldly life and stay in a state of balance and worship of the most severe kind. Penance is of three kinds : physical, spiritual or vocal.\nMonasticism is mentioned only once in the Holy Quran:\nوَجَعَلْنَا فِي قُلُوبِ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ رَأْفَةً وَرَحْمَةً وَرَهْبَانِيَّةً ابْتَدَعُوهَا مَا كَتَبْنَاهَا عَلَيْهِمْ إِلَّا ابْتِغَاءَ رِضْوَانِ اللَّهِ فَمَا رَعَوْهَا حَقَّ رِعَايَتِهَا\nAnd We placed in the hearts of those who followed him compassion and mercy and monasticism, which they innovated; We did not prescribe it for them except [that they did so] seeking the approval of Allah. But they did not observe it with due observance.\n(Quran, Surah-57, Al-Hadid, Verse-27)\nRahbaniyat(monasticism) is derived from the Arabic word ‘Rahab’ which means fear. That is, giving up the worldly life fearing the punishment of Allah(swt) is called ‘Rahbaniyat’. Every person cannot suppress his senses so he simply gives up this worldly life and lives a life of asceticism and penance.\nWe shall try to analyse how and why monasticism became popular among the Christians and why they could not follow it as mentioned in the Holy Quran.\nMonasticism was not preached by Isa(as). But till the third century many atrocities were committed against the Christians and in order to escape the tormentors, they escaped and hid in forests and caves. Here they had very little to eat and drink and slowly this took the form of asceticism.\nSecondly, the new converts to Christianity developed an aversion towards the worldly pleasures and indulgences of their old religion. And their scholars laid down rigid laws for them for leading their daily lives. And moreover they imbibed many customs from the Buddhist and Hindu monks and therefore it is not surprising that the principles found in the Christian books of monasticism are very much similar to those of Hindu jogis etc. For example abstaining from male-female inter-relations, subjecting the body to various types of pains, cutting-off parental relations, forsaking the worldly life and living in forests, caves etc. Monasticism in Christianity started in Egypt and Palestine and by the fourth century it had spread throughout Europe. St. Benedict, who himself was a great monk laid down the principles of monasticism. As mentioned earlier, monasticism was initially a necessity but slowly it became the sole means of earning the pleasure of Allah(swt). And then it came about that it became obligatory to follow monasticism. So, they laid down some rules for monks and a few of them are as follows:\nSubjecting oneself to pain. For example St. Macarius of Alexandria would always carry a weight of 40 pounds. For six months he lived in a marshy land where flies and mosquitoes tormented him. St. Benedict lived in a thorny forest for forty days and did not sleep on earth for forty years. St. John performed penance standing up for three years. Similarly, St. Simeon who was a popular monk of his time would fast for forty days at a time. He lived on one foot for one whole year. Some monks observed silence for thirty years. Some roamed about in forests and caves. Some ate grass and leaves.\nIt was also a custom of the monks to stay dirty. They would not bathe as they considered that a clean body means an unclean soul.\nIt was imperative for a monk to remain celibate and stay away from women. If he was already married, then he could not approach his wife. Having relations with a woman is considered a major sin. Similarly a woman monk should also remain unmarried and suppress her senses. For this they had to pass various tests. For example, a male and female monk would lie on the same cot but have their senses in total control. St. Evagrius describes the monks of Palestine who would bathe with women in the same room but have complete control over themselves. In the end all this penance, thoughts and knowledge could not endure the normal course of life and were subjugated by their senses and the monasteries became centres of indecency and obscenity. The Christian monks could not live up to the standards set by themselves and what we hear today about these monasteries is indeed sickening. Referring to this the Holy Quran says:\nوَجَعَلْنَا فِي قُلُوبِ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ رَأْفَةً وَرَحْمَةً وَرَهْبَانِيَّةً ابْتَدَعُوهَا مَا كَتَبْنَاهَا عَلَيْهِمْ إِلَّا ابْتِغَاءَ رِضْوَانِ اللَّهِ فَمَا رَعَوْهَا حَقَّ رِعَايَتِهَا\nAnd We placed in the hearts of those who followed him compassion and mercy and monasticism, which they innovated; We did not prescribe it for them except [that they did so] seeking the approval of Allah. But they did not observe it with due observance.\n(Quran, Surah-57, Al-Hadid, Verse-27)"]])